window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b051-b7b2ac1d3a2bd95a.json"]={sha256:"b7b2ac1d3a2bd95a4674767ef85e044e04703e0cc229f65edb27fbf11de62cec",value:{"id":"b051","title":"斜張索雨風振動抑制","titleEn":"Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"雨風振動是斜張索在中等風速與降雨同時出現時發生的大振幅振動，1980 年代在日本名港西大橋首次被系統記錄，之後在諾曼第大橋與伊拉斯謨大橋等通車初期都曾出現。本課從上緣水線的氣動機制、史庫頓數門檻、HDPE 套管的螺旋凸肋，到外置與內置阻尼器的選型、交叉索、現場監測、自由衰減驗收、錨口彎曲疲勞與阻尼器維護，建立從量測到對策與驗收的完整流程。","summaryEn":"Rain–wind vibration is a large-amplitude motion of stay cables that occurs when moderate wind and rain coincide; it was first systematically recorded on Japan’s Meiko-Nishi Bridge in the 1980s and later appeared soon after opening on bridges such as the Pont de Normandie and the Erasmus Bridge. The course builds a full workflow from measurement to remedy and acceptance: the aerodynamics of the upper rivulet, the Scruton number threshold, helical ribs on HDPE ducts, selection of external and internal dampers, cross-ties, field monitoring, free-decay acceptance, bending fatigue at the anchor exit and damper maintenance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-cable-stayed","subcategoryTitle":"斜張橋與斜索系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Cable-stayed bridges and stay systems","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-cable-stayed","learningTags":["structures","st-cable-stayed","cable"],"architectureFamily":"cable","architectureNodes":[["風雨與上緣水線","Wind, rain and upper rivulet"],["斜索與 HDPE 套管","Stay cable and HDPE duct"],["表面處理","Surface treatment"],["阻尼器與交叉索","Dampers and cross-ties"],["錨口與導向器","Anchor exit and deviator"],["監測、驗收與維護","Monitoring, acceptance and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[2,1],[3,1],[1,4],[3,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"cable","labels":["風雨與上緣水線","斜索與 HDPE 套管","表面處理","阻尼器與交叉索","錨口與導向器"],"labelsEn":["Wind, rain and upper rivulet","Stay cable and HDPE duct","Surface treatment","Dampers and cross-ties","Anchor exit and deviator"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：為一根長 300 m 的斜索選擇抑振方案。已知 m = 60 kg/m、D = 0.16 m、固有阻尼 ζ₀ = 0.15%，ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m，Sc₀ = 60×0.0015/0.032 ≈ 2.8，遠低於門檻約 10。方案 A：只用外置阻尼器，需 ζ ≥ 10×0.032/60 ≈ 0.53%，附加阻尼至少 0.38%，所需位置 x_d ≥ 2×0.0038×300 ≈ 2.3 m（以最佳係數計）；保留 50% 餘裕取 ζ_add = 0.57%，x_d ≈ 3.4 m。方案 B：採用螺旋凸肋套管，若試驗證明門檻可放寬到約 5，則需 ζ ≥ 5×0.032/60 ≈ 0.27%，附加阻尼 0.12% 即可，x_d ≈ 0.72 m，內置阻尼器就可能達到；代價是阻力係數若由 0.55 增至 0.6，50 m/s 下每根索的風力由約 1,531×0.55×0.16×300 ≈ 40.4 kN 增至約 44.1 kN（+9%）。若索長改為 450 m，方案 A 的位置需增至約 5.1 m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Design exercise: choose a suppression scheme for a 300 m stay with m = 60 kg/m, D = 0.16 m and inherent damping ζ₀ = 0.15%. With ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m, Sc₀ = 60×0.0015/0.032 ≈ 2.8, far below the threshold of about 10. Option A, external damper only: ζ ≥ 10×0.032/60 ≈ 0.53% requires at least 0.38% added damping, so the position is x_d ≥ 2×0.0038×300 ≈ 2.3 m at optimum coefficient; with 50% margin, ζ_add = 0.57% and x_d ≈ 3.4 m. Option B, helical-rib duct: if tests show the threshold can be relaxed to about 5, then ζ ≥ 5×0.032/60 ≈ 0.27% needs only 0.12% added damping and x_d ≈ 0.72 m, within reach of an internal damper; the price is drag rising from 0.55 to 0.6, so wind force per stay at 50 m/s goes from about 1,531×0.55×0.16×300 ≈ 40.4 kN to about 44.1 kN (+9%). For a 450 m stay, option A’s position grows to about 5.1 m. Values are teaching assumptions.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b051-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定」與「史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay\" and \"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b051-v13-01","title":"上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「上緣水線」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Upper water rivulet” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"乾燥的圓形斜索在一般風中很少大幅振動，因為圓形斷面沒有使振動自我放大的氣動力。下雨時，雨水沿傾斜的索面流下，在下緣與上緣各形成一條水線；上緣水線的位置由重力、表面張力與風的拖曳力共同決定，會隨索的振動在圓周方向來回移動。水線改變了斷面的有效形狀與氣流分離點，使氣動升力隨索的運動而變化，相位若恰好與速度同向，就等於負阻尼，把風的能量持續輸入索中。這種振動多發生在斜索沿風向往下傾斜、風速中等、雨量適中時，雨太大或太小、風太強都可能使水線無法穩定存在。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「上緣水線」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dry circular stay rarely vibrates heavily in ordinary wind, because a circular section produces no self-amplifying aerodynamic force. In rain, water running down the inclined surface forms rivulets along the lower and upper sides; the upper rivulet’s position, set by gravity, surface tension and wind drag, oscillates around the circumference as the cable moves. The rivulet changes the effective section shape and flow separation, so lift varies with cable motion; when it is in phase with velocity it acts as negative damping and keeps feeding wind energy into the cable. The vibration typically occurs on stays inclined downward in the wind direction, at moderate wind speed and moderate rainfall; too much or too little rain, or very strong wind, can prevent a stable rivulet. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Upper water rivulet” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：折算風速 U_r = U/(f·D)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Reduced velocity U_r = U/(f·D).","failure":"常見誤解：「雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「上緣水線」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Upper water rivulet”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-01-k1","title":"上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定","titleEn":"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay","text":"乾燥的圓形斜索在一般風中很少大幅振動，因為圓形斷面沒有使振動自我放大的氣動力。下雨時，雨水沿傾斜的索面流下，在下緣與上緣各形成一條水線；上緣水線的位置由重力、表面張力與風的拖曳力共同決定，會隨索的振動在圓周方向來回移動。","textEn":"A dry circular stay rarely vibrates heavily in ordinary wind, because a circular section produces no self-amplifying aerodynamic force. In rain, water running down the inclined surface forms rivulets along the lower and upper sides; the upper rivulet’s position, set by gravity, surface tension and wind drag, oscillates around the circumference as the cable moves.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay\" is correct?","options":["雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。","乾燥的圓形斜索在一般風中很少大幅振動，因為圓形斷面沒有使振動自我放大的氣動力。","斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。"],"optionsEn":["Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration.","A dry circular stay rarely vibrates heavily in ordinary wind, because a circular section produces no self-amplifying aerodynamic force.","Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"乾燥的圓形斜索在一般風中很少大幅振動，因為圓形斷面沒有使振動自我放大的氣動力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dry circular stay rarely vibrates heavily in ordinary wind, because a circular section produces no self-amplifying aerodynamic force. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b051-v13-02","title":"上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定：定量估算","titleEn":"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「上緣水線」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Upper water rivulet” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：折算風速 U_r = U/(f·D)。若 f = 1.2 Hz、D = 0.16 m，風速 U = 12 m/s 時 U_r = 12/(1.2×0.16) = 62.5；若觀測的發生風速範圍為 8 至 15 m/s，對應 U_r 約 42 至 78。以 U_r 表示可把不同索徑與頻率的觀測放在同一張圖比較。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Reduced velocity U_r = U/(f·D). With f = 1.2 Hz and D = 0.16 m, U = 12 m/s gives U_r = 12/(1.2×0.16) = 62.5; an observed onset range of 8 to 15 m/s corresponds to U_r of about 42 to 78. Expressing data as U_r lets cables of different diameters and frequencies be compared on one chart. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以風洞人工降雨試驗或現場同步紀錄（索加速度、風速風向、雨量）辨識振動發生的風速、風向與降雨區間，並以攝影確認上緣水線的存在與移動；把結果換成折算風速與相對風向角，與文獻中的發生區間比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Identify the wind speed, direction and rainfall range of onset by wind-tunnel tests with artificial rain or synchronised field records of cable acceleration, wind and rainfall, confirming the presence and motion of the upper rivulet by video; convert results to reduced velocity and relative yaw angle and compare with onset ranges in the literature.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"折算風速 U_r = U/(f·D)。若 f = 1.2 Hz、D = 0.16 m，風速 U = 12 m/s 時 U_r = 12/(1.2×0.16) = 62.5；若觀測的發生風速範圍為 8 至 15 m/s，對應 U_r 約 42 至 78。以 U_r 表示可把不同索徑與頻率的觀測放在同一張圖比較。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Reduced velocity U_r = U/(f·D). With f = 1.2 Hz and D = 0.16 m, U = 12 m/s gives U_r = 12/(1.2×0.16) = 62.5; an observed onset range of 8 to 15 m/s corresponds to U_r of about 42 to 78. Expressing data as U_r lets cables of different diameters and frequencies be compared on one chart. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。","內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。","折算風速 U_r = U/(f·D)。"],"optionsEn":["Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest.","Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.","Reduced velocity U_r = U/(f·D)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"折算風速 U_r = U/(f·D)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Reduced velocity U_r = U/(f·D). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b051-v13-03","title":"上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「上緣水線」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Upper water rivulet” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以風洞人工降雨試驗或現場同步紀錄（索加速度、風速風向、雨量）辨識振動發生的風速、風向與降雨區間，並以攝影確認上緣水線的存在與移動；把結果換成折算風速與相對風向角，與文獻中的發生區間比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Identify the wind speed, direction and rainfall range of onset by wind-tunnel tests with artificial rain or synchronised field records of cable acceleration, wind and rainfall, confirming the presence and motion of the upper rivulet by video; convert results to reduced velocity and relative yaw angle and compare with onset ranges in the literature. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：斜張橋設計階段就要依索的傾角、方位與當地盛行風雨評估雨風振動風險，並在設計報告中列出每組索的對策（表面處理、阻尼、交叉索）與預留空間。","observationEn":"Site practice: At design stage, assess rain–wind risk from each stay’s inclination, orientation and the local prevailing wind and rain, and list in the design report the remedy for each stay group (surface treatment, damping, cross-ties) with space reserved.","failure":"注意干擾：若把雨風振動誤判為一般渦振而只加裝針對高頻的小型阻尼，振動仍會在下一場風雨中出現；長期大振幅使錨口彎曲疲勞、套管與防水帽磨損，並引起使用者恐慌與交通管制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Misreading rain–wind vibration as ordinary vortex shedding and fitting only small high-frequency dampers leaves it to return in the next rainstorm; sustained large amplitudes cause bending fatigue at the anchor exit, wear ducts and caps, alarm users and force traffic restrictions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以風洞人工降雨試驗或現場同步紀錄（索加速度、風速風向、雨量）辨識振動發生的風速、風向與降雨區間，並以攝影確認上緣水線的存在與移動；把結果換成折算風速與相對風向角，與文獻中的發生區間比較。","textEn":"Identify the wind speed, direction and rainfall range of onset by wind-tunnel tests with artificial rain or synchronised field records of cable acceleration, wind and rainfall, confirming the presence and motion of the upper rivulet by video; convert results to reduced velocity and relative yaw angle and compare with onset ranges in the literature.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"斜張橋設計階段就要依索的傾角、方位與當地盛行風雨評估雨風振動風險，並在設計報告中列出每組索的對策（表面處理、阻尼、交叉索）與預留空間。","textEn":"At design stage, assess rain–wind risk from each stay’s inclination, orientation and the local prevailing wind and rain, and list in the design report the remedy for each stay group (surface treatment, damping, cross-ties) with space reserved.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay\"?","options":["以風洞人工降雨試驗或現場同步紀錄（索加速度、風速風向、雨量）辨識振動發生的風速、風向與降雨區間，並以攝影確認上緣水線的存在與移動。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。"],"optionsEn":["Identify the wind speed, direction and rainfall range of onset by wind-tunnel tests with artificial rain or synchronised field records of cable acceleration, wind and rainfall, confirming the presence and motion of the upper rivulet by video.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以風洞人工降雨試驗或現場同步紀錄（索加速度、風速風向、雨量）辨識振動發生的風速、風向與降雨區間，並以攝影確認上緣水線的存在與移動；把結果換成折算風速與相對風向角，與文獻中的發生區間比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Identify the wind speed, direction and rainfall range of onset by wind-tunnel tests with artificial rain or synchronised field records of cable acceleration, wind and rainfall, confirming the presence and motion of the upper rivulet by video; convert results to reduced velocity and relative yaw angle and compare with onset ranges in the literature. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b051-v13-04","title":"上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定：失效診斷","titleEn":"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「上緣水線」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Upper water rivulet” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把雨風振動誤判為一般渦振而只加裝針對高頻的小型阻尼，振動仍會在下一場風雨中出現；長期大振幅使錨口彎曲疲勞、套管與防水帽磨損，並引起使用者恐慌與交通管制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Misreading rain–wind vibration as ordinary vortex shedding and fitting only small high-frequency dampers leaves it to return in the next rainstorm; sustained large amplitudes cause bending fatigue at the anchor exit, wear ducts and caps, alarm users and force traffic restrictions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這種振動多發生在斜索沿風向往下傾斜、風速中等、雨量適中時，雨太大或太小、風太強都可能使水線無法穩定存在。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The vibration typically occurs on stays inclined downward in the wind direction, at moderate wind speed and moderate rainfall; too much or too little rain, or very strong wind, can prevent a stable rivulet.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把雨風振動誤判為一般渦振而只加裝針對高頻的小型阻尼，振動仍會在下一場風雨中出現；長期大振幅使錨口彎曲疲勞、套管與防水帽磨損，並引起使用者恐慌與交通管制。","textEn":"Misreading rain–wind vibration as ordinary vortex shedding and fitting only small high-frequency dampers leaves it to return in the next rainstorm; sustained large amplitudes cause bending fatigue at the anchor exit, wear ducts and caps, alarm users and force traffic restrictions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「上緣水線如何讓圓形斜索不穩定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"How an upper rivulet destabilises a circular stay\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若把雨風振動誤判為一般渦振而只加裝針對高頻的小型阻尼，振動仍會在下一場風雨中出現；長期大振幅使錨口彎曲疲勞、套管與防水帽磨損，並引起使用者恐慌與交通管制。","斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Misreading rain–wind vibration as ordinary vortex shedding and fitting only small high-frequency dampers leaves it to return in the next rainstorm.","Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若把雨風振動誤判為一般渦振而只加裝針對高頻的小型阻尼，振動仍會在下一場風雨中出現；長期大振幅使錨口彎曲疲勞、套管與防水帽磨損，並引起使用者恐慌與交通管制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Misreading rain–wind vibration as ordinary vortex shedding and fitting only small high-frequency dampers leaves it to return in the next rainstorm; sustained large amplitudes cause bending fatigue at the anchor exit, wear ducts and caps, alarm users and force traffic restrictions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b051-v13-05","title":"史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「史庫頓數」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Scruton number” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"史庫頓數 Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) 把索的單位長度質量 m、阻尼比 ζ 與空氣密度 ρ、索徑 D 合成一個無因次數，表示結構消耗能量的能力相對於氣流能輸入的能量。Sc 越大，雨風振動與渦振越不容易發展。長斜索的固有阻尼通常只有千分之一到千分之幾，Sc 往往只有個位數；工程上常被引用的門檻約為 10，表面經過有效處理時可放寬。由於 m 與 D 由結構需要決定，工程師真正能調整的是阻尼比，因此 Sc 準則直接轉化為「需要多少附加阻尼」的設計目標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「史庫頓數」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Scruton number Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) combines mass per metre m, damping ratio ζ, air density ρ and diameter D into a dimensionless measure of the structure’s ability to dissipate energy relative to what the flow can feed in. The larger Sc, the less likely rain–wind or vortex vibration can develop. Long stays usually have inherent damping of only one to a few thousandths, giving Sc in single figures; a commonly cited threshold is about 10, relaxable where effective surface treatment is used. Since m and D are fixed by structural needs, the variable engineers can really change is damping, so the Sc criterion becomes a target for added damping. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Scruton number” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：取 m = 60 kg/m、D = 0.16 m、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³，ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With m = 60 kg/m, D = 0.16 m and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³, ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「史庫頓數」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Scruton number”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-05-k1","title":"史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入","titleEn":"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input","text":"史庫頓數 Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) 把索的單位長度質量 m、阻尼比 ζ 與空氣密度 ρ、索徑 D 合成一個無因次數，表示結構消耗能量的能力相對於氣流能輸入的能量。Sc 越大，雨風振動與渦振越不容易發展。","textEn":"The Scruton number Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) combines mass per metre m, damping ratio ζ, air density ρ and diameter D into a dimensionless measure of the structure’s ability to dissipate energy relative to what the flow can feed in. The larger Sc, the less likely rain–wind or vortex vibration can develop.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input\" is correct?","options":["斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。","套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。","史庫頓數 Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) 把索的單位長度質量 m、阻尼比 ζ 與空氣密度 ρ、索徑 D 合成一個無因次數，表示結構消耗能量的能力相對於氣流能輸入的能量。"],"optionsEn":["Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration.","The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.","The Scruton number Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) combines mass per metre m, damping ratio ζ, air density ρ and diameter D into a dimensionless measure of the structure’s ability to dissipate energy relative to what the flow can feed in."],"answer":2,"explanation":"史庫頓數 Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) 把索的單位長度質量 m、阻尼比 ζ 與空氣密度 ρ、索徑 D 合成一個無因次數，表示結構消耗能量的能力相對於氣流能輸入的能量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Scruton number Sc = m·ζ/(ρ·D²) combines mass per metre m, damping ratio ζ, air density ρ and diameter D into a dimensionless measure of the structure’s ability to dissipate energy relative to what the flow can feed in. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b051-v13-06","title":"史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入：定量估算","titleEn":"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「史庫頓數」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Scruton number” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：取 m = 60 kg/m、D = 0.16 m、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³，ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m。固有阻尼 ζ = 0.2% 時 Sc = 60×0.002/0.032 = 3.75；要達到 Sc = 10，需 ζ = 10×0.032/60 ≈ 0.53%，即至少增加約 0.33% 的附加阻尼。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With m = 60 kg/m, D = 0.16 m and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³, ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m. Inherent damping ζ = 0.2% gives Sc = 60×0.002/0.032 = 3.75; reaching Sc = 10 needs ζ = 10×0.032/60 ≈ 0.53%, at least about 0.33% of added damping. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以自由衰減試驗量測每組代表性斜索的固有阻尼（未裝阻尼器時），計算 Sc 並與門檻比較；裝阻尼器後再量一次，確認 Sc 達標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure inherent damping of representative stays in each group by free decay before dampers are fitted, compute Sc against the threshold, then measure again after fitting to confirm compliance; cover the several modes most likely to be excited, because one damper gives different damping in different modes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"取 m = 60 kg/m、D = 0.16 m、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³，ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m。固有阻尼 ζ = 0.2% 時 Sc = 60×0.002/0.032 = 3.75；要達到 Sc = 10，需 ζ = 10×0.032/60 ≈ 0.53%，即至少增加約 0.33% 的附加阻尼。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With m = 60 kg/m, D = 0.16 m and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³, ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m. Inherent damping ζ = 0.2% gives Sc = 60×0.002/0.032 = 3.75; reaching Sc = 10 needs ζ = 10×0.032/60 ≈ 0.53%, at least about 0.33% of added damping. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input\", which statement holds?","options":["取 m = 60 kg/m、D = 0.16 m、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³，ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m。","交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。","只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。"],"optionsEn":["With m = 60 kg/m, D = 0.16 m and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³, ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m.","Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation.","An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"取 m = 60 kg/m、D = 0.16 m、ρ = 1.25 kg/m³，ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With m = 60 kg/m, D = 0.16 m and ρ = 1.25 kg/m³, ρ·D² = 0.032 kg/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b051-v13-07","title":"史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「史庫頓數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Scruton number” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以自由衰減試驗量測每組代表性斜索的固有阻尼（未裝阻尼器時），計算 Sc 並與門檻比較；裝阻尼器後再量一次，確認 Sc 達標。量測要涵蓋最可能被激發的數個模態，因為同一阻尼器在不同模態提供的阻尼不同。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure inherent damping of representative stays in each group by free decay before dampers are fitted, compute Sc against the threshold, then measure again after fitting to confirm compliance; cover the several modes most likely to be excited, because one damper gives different damping in different modes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：斜索規格書應以 Sc 或最低對數遞減率表示阻尼要求，並註明適用的模態範圍與量測方法；驗收報告須逐組列出量測的阻尼與計算的 Sc。","observationEn":"Site practice: The stay specification should express damping requirements as Sc or a minimum logarithmic decrement, state the applicable mode range and test method, and the acceptance report should list measured damping and computed Sc for each group.","failure":"注意干擾：若以設計假設的固有阻尼（例如 0.5%）計算 Sc 而不量測，實際只有 0.1% 至 0.2% 時，振動仍會發生；阻尼器只針對第一模態最佳化，較高模態的 Sc 可能仍低於門檻。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Computing Sc from an assumed inherent damping such as 0.5% without measurement, when the real value is only 0.1% to 0.2%, leaves vibration to occur; a damper optimised only for mode 1 can leave higher modes below the threshold. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以自由衰減試驗量測每組代表性斜索的固有阻尼（未裝阻尼器時），計算 Sc 並與門檻比較；裝阻尼器後再量一次，確認 Sc 達標。量測要涵蓋最可能被激發的數個模態，因為同一阻尼器在不同模態提供的阻尼不同。","textEn":"Measure inherent damping of representative stays in each group by free decay before dampers are fitted, compute Sc against the threshold, then measure again after fitting to confirm compliance; cover the several modes most likely to be excited, because one damper gives different damping in different modes.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"斜索規格書應以 Sc 或最低對數遞減率表示阻尼要求，並註明適用的模態範圍與量測方法；驗收報告須逐組列出量測的阻尼與計算的 Sc。","textEn":"The stay specification should express damping requirements as Sc or a minimum logarithmic decrement, state the applicable mode range and test method, and the acceptance report should list measured damping and computed Sc for each group.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以自由衰減試驗量測每組代表性斜索的固有阻尼（未裝阻尼器時），計算 Sc 並與門檻比較；裝阻尼器後再量一次，確認 Sc 達標。","斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Measure inherent damping of representative stays in each group by free decay before dampers are fitted, compute Sc against the threshold, then measure again after fitting to confirm compliance.","Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以自由衰減試驗量測每組代表性斜索的固有阻尼（未裝阻尼器時），計算 Sc 並與門檻比較；裝阻尼器後再量一次，確認 Sc 達標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure inherent damping of representative stays in each group by free decay before dampers are fitted, compute Sc against the threshold, then measure again after fitting to confirm compliance; cover the several modes most likely to be excited, because one damper gives different damping in different modes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b051-v13-08","title":"史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入：失效診斷","titleEn":"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「史庫頓數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Scruton number” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若以設計假設的固有阻尼（例如 0.5%）計算 Sc 而不量測，實際只有 0.1% 至 0.2% 時，振動仍會發生；阻尼器只針對第一模態最佳化，較高模態的 Sc 可能仍低於門檻。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Computing Sc from an assumed inherent damping such as 0.5% without measurement, when the real value is only 0.1% to 0.2%, leaves vibration to occur; a damper optimised only for mode 1 can leave higher modes below the threshold. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：由於 m 與 D 由結構需要決定，工程師真正能調整的是阻尼比，因此 Sc 準則直接轉化為「需要多少附加阻尼」的設計目標。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Since m and D are fixed by structural needs, the variable engineers can really change is damping, so the Sc criterion becomes a target for added damping.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若以設計假設的固有阻尼（例如 0.5%）計算 Sc 而不量測，實際只有 0.1% 至 0.2% 時，振動仍會發生；阻尼器只針對第一模態最佳化，較高模態的 Sc 可能仍低於門檻。","textEn":"Computing Sc from an assumed inherent damping such as 0.5% without measurement, when the real value is only 0.1% to 0.2%, leaves vibration to occur; a damper optimised only for mode 1 can leave higher modes below the threshold.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「史庫頓數：用質量與阻尼對抗氣動輸入」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The Scruton number: mass and damping against aerodynamic input\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。","若以設計假設的固有阻尼（例如 0.5%）計算 Sc 而不量測，實際只有 0.1% 至 0.2% 時，振動仍會發生。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.","Computing Sc from an assumed inherent damping such as 0.5% without measurement, when the real value is only 0.1% to 0.2%, leaves vibration to occur."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若以設計假設的固有阻尼（例如 0.5%）計算 Sc 而不量測，實際只有 0.1% 至 0.2% 時，振動仍會發生；阻尼器只針對第一模態最佳化，較高模態的 Sc 可能仍低於門檻。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Computing Sc from an assumed inherent damping such as 0.5% without measurement, when the real value is only 0.1% to 0.2%, leaves vibration to occur; a damper optimised only for mode 1 can leave higher modes below the threshold. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b051-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩」與「外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples\" and \"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b051-v13-09","title":"套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「雙螺旋凸肋套管」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Double-helix ribbed duct” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"既然雨風振動仰賴穩定的上緣水線，最直接的對策就是讓水線無法形成。常見做法是在 HDPE 外套管表面擠出雙螺旋凸肋，雨水被凸肋打斷、沿螺旋方向分散流下；另一種做法是在表面壓出凹窩或其他紋理。供應商公開資料指出其主套管以雙螺旋凸紋打斷水流以限制雨風振動，阻力係數約 0.6；里翁—安提里翁大橋的斜索也以螺旋凸條保護。表面處理不需要維護機構，但會增加套管的風阻，使塔與橋面承受更大的風荷載，凸肋的高度與螺距需要在抑振與阻力之間取捨。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「雙螺旋凸肋套管」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Since rain–wind vibration depends on a stable upper rivulet, the most direct remedy is to stop it forming. A common approach extrudes a double helical rib on the HDPE outer duct, breaking up rainwater so it spreads along the spiral; another presses dimples or other textures into the surface. A supplier states that its main duct uses double spiral threads to disrupt water flow and limit rain–wind vibration, with a drag coefficient of about 0.6, and the Rion–Antirion stays are likewise protected by spiral strakes. Surface treatment has no mechanism to maintain but raises duct drag, increasing wind load on pylon and deck, so rib height and pitch trade suppression against drag. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Double-helix ribbed duct” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：斜索風力 F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Stay wind force F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L.","failure":"常見誤解：「套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「雙螺旋凸肋套管」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Double-helix ribbed duct”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-09-k1","title":"套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩","titleEn":"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples","text":"既然雨風振動仰賴穩定的上緣水線，最直接的對策就是讓水線無法形成。常見做法是在 HDPE 外套管表面擠出雙螺旋凸肋，雨水被凸肋打斷、沿螺旋方向分散流下；另一種做法是在表面壓出凹窩或其他紋理。","textEn":"Since rain–wind vibration depends on a stable upper rivulet, the most direct remedy is to stop it forming. A common approach extrudes a double helical rib on the HDPE outer duct, breaking up rainwater so it spreads along the spiral; another presses dimples or other textures into the surface.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples\" is correct?","options":["既然雨風振動仰賴穩定的上緣水線，最直接的對策就是讓水線無法形成。","套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。","阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Since rain–wind vibration depends on a stable upper rivulet, the most direct remedy is to stop it forming.","The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.","Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest."],"answer":0,"explanation":"既然雨風振動仰賴穩定的上緣水線，最直接的對策就是讓水線無法形成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Since rain–wind vibration depends on a stable upper rivulet, the most direct remedy is to stop it forming. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b051-v13-10","title":"套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩：定量估算","titleEn":"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙螺旋凸肋套管」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Double-helix ribbed duct” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：斜索風力 F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L。U = 50 m/s（q ≈ 1,531 Pa）、D = 0.2 m、L = 300 m：C_D = 0.6 時 F ≈ 1,531×0.6×0.2×300 ≈ 55.1 kN；若處理不當使 C_D = 0.75，F ≈ 68.9 kN，增加 25%，全橋數百根索累積後對塔與橋面不可忽視。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Stay wind force F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L. With U = 50 m/s (q ≈ 1,531 Pa), D = 0.2 m and L = 300 m, C_D = 0.6 gives F ≈ 1,531×0.6×0.2×300 ≈ 55.1 kN; a poorly chosen treatment with C_D = 0.75 gives F ≈ 68.9 kN, 25% more, which summed over hundreds of stays is significant for pylon and deck. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以足尺或大比例的套管段在風洞中做人工降雨試驗，確認在發生區間內不再出現大振幅；同時量測不同雷諾數下的阻力係數，並把結果用於全橋風荷載計算。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Test full-scale or large-scale duct sections with artificial rain in a wind tunnel to confirm no large amplitudes within the onset range, measuring drag coefficients across Reynolds numbers for use in global wind loads; confirm by monitoring that amplitudes stay controlled in wind–rain events after opening.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"斜索風力 F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L。U = 50 m/s（q ≈ 1,531 Pa）、D = 0.2 m、L = 300 m：C_D = 0.6 時 F ≈ 1,531×0.6×0.2×300 ≈ 55.1 kN；若處理不當使 C_D = 0.75，F ≈ 68.9 kN，增加 25%，全橋數百根索累積後對塔與橋面不可忽視。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Stay wind force F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L. With U = 50 m/s (q ≈ 1,531 Pa), D = 0.2 m and L = 300 m, C_D = 0.6 gives F ≈ 1,531×0.6×0.2×300 ≈ 55.1 kN; a poorly chosen treatment with C_D = 0.75 gives F ≈ 68.9 kN, 25% more, which summed over hundreds of stays is significant for pylon and deck. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples\", which statement holds?","options":["內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。","斜索風力 F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L。","阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。"],"optionsEn":["Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.","Stay wind force F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L.","A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斜索風力 F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Stay wind force F = ½ρU²·C_D·D·L. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b051-v13-11","title":"套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙螺旋凸肋套管」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Double-helix ribbed duct” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以足尺或大比例的套管段在風洞中做人工降雨試驗，確認在發生區間內不再出現大振幅；同時量測不同雷諾數下的阻力係數，並把結果用於全橋風荷載計算。現場以監測確認通車後的風雨事件中振幅受控。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Test full-scale or large-scale duct sections with artificial rain in a wind tunnel to confirm no large amplitudes within the onset range, measuring drag coefficients across Reynolds numbers for use in global wind loads; confirm by monitoring that amplitudes stay controlled in wind–rain events after opening. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：套管表面處理的選擇要同時附上抑振試驗與阻力試驗報告，並在全橋設計中採用相同的阻力係數；安裝時檢查凸肋連續性與接頭方向，損傷段須依供應商程序修補，例如補焊螺旋凸條。","observationEn":"Site practice: Select duct treatments with both suppression and drag test reports and use the same drag coefficient in global design; during installation check rib continuity and joint orientation, repairing damaged lengths under the supplier’s procedure such as post-welding helical fillets.","failure":"注意干擾：凸肋在運輸或安裝時被磨損、套管接頭處凸肋不連續，局部仍可能形成水線；若只看抑振效果而未計入增加的阻力，塔與橋面的風荷載與疲勞會被低估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ribs worn in transport or installation, or discontinuous at duct joints, can still allow local rivulets; judging only vibration suppression without counting the extra drag underestimates wind load and fatigue on pylon and deck. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以足尺或大比例的套管段在風洞中做人工降雨試驗，確認在發生區間內不再出現大振幅；同時量測不同雷諾數下的阻力係數，並把結果用於全橋風荷載計算。現場以監測確認通車後的風雨事件中振幅受控。","textEn":"Test full-scale or large-scale duct sections with artificial rain in a wind tunnel to confirm no large amplitudes within the onset range, measuring drag coefficients across Reynolds numbers for use in global wind loads; confirm by monitoring that amplitudes stay controlled in wind–rain events after opening.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"套管表面處理的選擇要同時附上抑振試驗與阻力試驗報告，並在全橋設計中採用相同的阻力係數；安裝時檢查凸肋連續性與接頭方向，損傷段須依供應商程序修補，例如補焊螺旋凸條。","textEn":"Select duct treatments with both suppression and drag test reports and use the same drag coefficient in global design; during installation check rib continuity and joint orientation, repairing damaged lengths under the supplier’s procedure such as post-welding helical fillets.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。","以足尺或大比例的套管段在風洞中做人工降雨試驗，確認在發生區間內不再出現大振幅；同時量測不同雷諾數下的阻力係數，並把結果用於全橋風荷載計算。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed.","Test full-scale or large-scale duct sections with artificial rain in a wind tunnel to confirm no large amplitudes within the onset range, measuring drag coefficients across Reynolds numbers for use in global wind loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以足尺或大比例的套管段在風洞中做人工降雨試驗，確認在發生區間內不再出現大振幅；同時量測不同雷諾數下的阻力係數，並把結果用於全橋風荷載計算。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Test full-scale or large-scale duct sections with artificial rain in a wind tunnel to confirm no large amplitudes within the onset range, measuring drag coefficients across Reynolds numbers for use in global wind loads; confirm by monitoring that amplitudes stay controlled in wind–rain events after opening. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b051-v13-12","title":"套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩：失效診斷","titleEn":"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙螺旋凸肋套管」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Double-helix ribbed duct” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"凸肋在運輸或安裝時被磨損、套管接頭處凸肋不連續，局部仍可能形成水線；若只看抑振效果而未計入增加的阻力，塔與橋面的風荷載與疲勞會被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ribs worn in transport or installation, or discontinuous at duct joints, can still allow local rivulets; judging only vibration suppression without counting the extra drag underestimates wind load and fatigue on pylon and deck. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：表面處理不需要維護機構，但會增加套管的風阻，使塔與橋面承受更大的風荷載，凸肋的高度與螺距需要在抑振與阻力之間取捨。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface treatment has no mechanism to maintain but raises duct drag, increasing wind load on pylon and deck, so rib height and pitch trade suppression against drag.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"凸肋在運輸或安裝時被磨損、套管接頭處凸肋不連續，局部仍可能形成水線；若只看抑振效果而未計入增加的阻力，塔與橋面的風荷載與疲勞會被低估。","textEn":"Ribs worn in transport or installation, or discontinuous at duct joints, can still allow local rivulets; judging only vibration suppression without counting the extra drag underestimates wind load and fatigue on pylon and deck.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「套管表面處理：螺旋凸肋與凹窩」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Duct surface treatment: helical ribs and dimples\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["凸肋在運輸或安裝時被磨損、套管接頭處凸肋不連續，局部仍可能形成水線；若只看抑振效果而未計入增加的阻力，塔與橋面的風荷載與疲勞會被低估。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Ribs worn in transport or installation, or discontinuous at duct joints, can still allow local rivulets.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest."],"answer":0,"explanation":"凸肋在運輸或安裝時被磨損、套管接頭處凸肋不連續，局部仍可能形成水線；若只看抑振效果而未計入增加的阻力，塔與橋面的風荷載與疲勞會被低估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ribs worn in transport or installation, or discontinuous at duct joints, can still allow local rivulets; judging only vibration suppression without counting the extra drag underestimates wind load and fatigue on pylon and deck. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b051-v13-13","title":"外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「外置黏滯阻尼器」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “External viscous damper” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外置阻尼器裝在斜索與橋面（或塔）之間，以一支黏滯阻尼器連接索上某點與固定支架。張緊弦理論顯示，阻尼器能提供的最大附加阻尼比約為阻尼器到錨點距離佔索長比例的一半，且只有在阻尼係數最佳時才達到。長索需要的阻尼器位置因此可能離橋面數公尺，要靠高支架或控制桅桿支撐。供應商公開案例中，亞武茲蘇丹塞利姆大橋使用 7.4 m 高的控制桅桿支撐行程 ±920 mm 的油壓活塞，正反映超長索對阻尼器位置與行程的需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外置黏滯阻尼器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An external damper links a point on the stay to a fixed bracket on the deck or pylon through a viscous unit. Taut-string theory shows that the maximum added damping ratio is about half the damper’s distance from the anchorage as a fraction of cable length, reached only at the optimum coefficient. Long stays may therefore need dampers several metres above the deck on tall brackets or control masts. In a supplier’s public case, the Yavuz Sultan Selim Bridge uses 7.4 m control masts carrying hydraulic pistons with ±920 mm stroke, illustrating what very long stays demand of damper position and stroke. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “External viscous damper” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：最大附加阻尼 ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Maximum added damping ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L).","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外置黏滯阻尼器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “External viscous damper”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-13-k1","title":"外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼","titleEn":"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping","text":"外置阻尼器裝在斜索與橋面（或塔）之間，以一支黏滯阻尼器連接索上某點與固定支架。張緊弦理論顯示，阻尼器能提供的最大附加阻尼比約為阻尼器到錨點距離佔索長比例的一半，且只有在阻尼係數最佳時才達到。","textEn":"An external damper links a point on the stay to a fixed bracket on the deck or pylon through a viscous unit. Taut-string theory shows that the maximum added damping ratio is about half the damper’s distance from the anchorage as a fraction of cable length, reached only at the optimum coefficient.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。","外置阻尼器裝在斜索與橋面（或塔）之間，以一支黏滯阻尼器連接索上某點與固定支架。","交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest.","An external damper links a point on the stay to a fixed bracket on the deck or pylon through a viscous unit.","Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外置阻尼器裝在斜索與橋面（或塔）之間，以一支黏滯阻尼器連接索上某點與固定支架。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An external damper links a point on the stay to a fixed bracket on the deck or pylon through a viscous unit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b051-v13-14","title":"外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼：定量估算","titleEn":"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外置黏滯阻尼器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “External viscous damper” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：最大附加阻尼 ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L)。要達到單元 2 的 0.53%，需 x_d/L ≥ 2×0.0053 ≈ 1.07%；索長 L = 400 m 時 x_d ≈ 0.0107×400 ≈ 4.3 m。若橋面空間只允許 2.5 m，ζ_max ≈ 2.5/800 ≈ 0.31%，不足，需加交叉索或表面處理。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Maximum added damping ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L). Reaching unit 2’s 0.53% needs x_d/L ≥ 2×0.0053 ≈ 1.07%; for L = 400 m, x_d ≈ 0.0107×400 ≈ 4.3 m. If deck space allows only 2.5 m, ζ_max ≈ 2.5/800 ≈ 0.31%, not enough, so cross-ties or surface treatment are needed as well. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：阻尼器出廠做力—速度、行程與耐久試驗；安裝後以人工激振做自由衰減，比較有無阻尼器時的阻尼比；支架本身以模態量測確認勁度足夠，避免支架振動吃掉阻尼器的行程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Factory-test dampers for force–velocity, stroke and endurance; after installation run free-decay tests by manual excitation, comparing damping with and without the damper; confirm by modal measurement that the bracket itself is stiff enough so its own motion does not consume damper stroke.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"最大附加阻尼 ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L)。要達到單元 2 的 0.53%，需 x_d/L ≥ 2×0.0053 ≈ 1.07%；索長 L = 400 m 時 x_d ≈ 0.0107×400 ≈ 4.3 m。若橋面空間只允許 2.5 m，ζ_max ≈ 2.5/800 ≈ 0.31%，不足，需加交叉索或表面處理。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Maximum added damping ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L). Reaching unit 2’s 0.53% needs x_d/L ≥ 2×0.0053 ≈ 1.07%; for L = 400 m, x_d ≈ 0.0107×400 ≈ 4.3 m. If deck space allows only 2.5 m, ζ_max ≈ 2.5/800 ≈ 0.31%, not enough, so cross-ties or surface treatment are needed as well. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping\", which statement holds?","options":["只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。","斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。","最大附加阻尼 ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L)。"],"optionsEn":["An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration.","Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.","Maximum added damping ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最大附加阻尼 ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Maximum added damping ζ_max ≈ x_d/(2L). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b051-v13-15","title":"外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外置黏滯阻尼器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “External viscous damper” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"阻尼器出廠做力—速度、行程與耐久試驗；安裝後以人工激振做自由衰減，比較有無阻尼器時的阻尼比；支架本身以模態量測確認勁度足夠，避免支架振動吃掉阻尼器的行程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Factory-test dampers for force–velocity, stroke and endurance; after installation run free-decay tests by manual excitation, comparing damping with and without the damper; confirm by modal measurement that the bracket itself is stiff enough so its own motion does not consume damper stroke. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：阻尼器配置圖要標示每根索的阻尼器位置比例、設計係數、行程與支架勁度要求；任何因景觀或交通需求而降低阻尼器高度的變更，都要重新計算可達阻尼並由設計者核可。","observationEn":"Site practice: The damper layout should show each stay’s position ratio, design coefficient, stroke and bracket stiffness; any change lowering damper height for appearance or traffic must recompute achievable damping and be approved by the designer.","failure":"注意干擾：支架勁度不足時，阻尼器兩端一起移動，實際消能遠低於理論；係數偏離最佳值太多，阻尼器變成近似固定點或幾乎不受力，附加阻尼都很小。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A flexible bracket moves with the damper so actual dissipation falls far below theory; a coefficient far from optimum makes the damper act almost as a fixed point or barely engaged, and added damping is small either way. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"阻尼器出廠做力—速度、行程與耐久試驗；安裝後以人工激振做自由衰減，比較有無阻尼器時的阻尼比；支架本身以模態量測確認勁度足夠，避免支架振動吃掉阻尼器的行程。","textEn":"Factory-test dampers for force–velocity, stroke and endurance; after installation run free-decay tests by manual excitation, comparing damping with and without the damper; confirm by modal measurement that the bracket itself is stiff enough so its own motion does not consume damper stroke.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"阻尼器配置圖要標示每根索的阻尼器位置比例、設計係數、行程與支架勁度要求；任何因景觀或交通需求而降低阻尼器高度的變更，都要重新計算可達阻尼並由設計者核可。","textEn":"The damper layout should show each stay’s position ratio, design coefficient, stroke and bracket stiffness; any change lowering damper height for appearance or traffic must recompute achievable damping and be approved by the designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping\"?","options":["阻尼器出廠做力—速度、行程與耐久試驗；安裝後以人工激振做自由衰減，比較有無阻尼器時的阻尼比；支架本身以模態量測確認勁度足夠，避免支架振動吃掉阻尼器的行程。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。"],"optionsEn":["Factory-test dampers for force–velocity, stroke and endurance.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼器出廠做力—速度、行程與耐久試驗；安裝後以人工激振做自由衰減，比較有無阻尼器時的阻尼比；支架本身以模態量測確認勁度足夠，避免支架振動吃掉阻尼器的行程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Factory-test dampers for force–velocity, stroke and endurance; after installation run free-decay tests by manual excitation, comparing damping with and without the damper; confirm by modal measurement that the bracket itself is stiff enough so its own motion does not consume damper stroke. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b051-v13-16","title":"外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼：失效診斷","titleEn":"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外置黏滯阻尼器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “External viscous damper” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支架勁度不足時，阻尼器兩端一起移動，實際消能遠低於理論；係數偏離最佳值太多，阻尼器變成近似固定點或幾乎不受力，附加阻尼都很小。高支架若設計不當，本身也可能成為新的振動源。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A flexible bracket moves with the damper so actual dissipation falls far below theory; a coefficient far from optimum makes the damper act almost as a fixed point or barely engaged, and added damping is small either way. A poorly designed tall mast can itself become a new source of vibration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：供應商公開案例中，亞武茲蘇丹塞利姆大橋使用 7.4 m 高的控制桅桿支撐行程 ±920 mm 的油壓活塞，正反映超長索對阻尼器位置與行程的需求。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In a supplier’s public case, the Yavuz Sultan Selim Bridge uses 7.4 m control masts carrying hydraulic pistons with ±920 mm stroke, illustrating what very long stays demand of damper position and stroke.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支架勁度不足時，阻尼器兩端一起移動，實際消能遠低於理論；係數偏離最佳值太多，阻尼器變成近似固定點或幾乎不受力，附加阻尼都很小。高支架若設計不當，本身也可能成為新的振動源。","textEn":"A flexible bracket moves with the damper so actual dissipation falls far below theory; a coefficient far from optimum makes the damper act almost as a fixed point or barely engaged, and added damping is small either way. A poorly designed tall mast can itself become a new source of vibration.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外置阻尼器的位置、係數與可達阻尼」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"External damper position, coefficient and achievable damping\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","支架勁度不足時，阻尼器兩端一起移動，實際消能遠低於理論；係數偏離最佳值太多，阻尼器變成近似固定點或幾乎不受力，附加阻尼都很小。","交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A flexible bracket moves with the damper so actual dissipation falls far below theory.","Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支架勁度不足時，阻尼器兩端一起移動，實際消能遠低於理論；係數偏離最佳值太多，阻尼器變成近似固定點或幾乎不受力，附加阻尼都很小。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A flexible bracket moves with the damper so actual dissipation falls far below theory; a coefficient far from optimum makes the damper act almost as a fixed point or barely engaged, and added damping is small either way. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b051-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「交叉索：把單根長索變成索網」與「內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network\" and \"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b051-v13-17","title":"交叉索：把單根長索變成索網：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「交叉索」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cross-ties” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"交叉索是在同一索面相鄰斜索之間加裝細索或連桿，把它們連成網。單根長索被分成較短的段落，低階模態的頻率提高，原本容易被雨風或橋面運動激發的低頻振動被移到較高頻率；不同斜索的頻率也不再各自獨立，彼此牽制，振動能量在網中分散。供應商公開資料把交叉索列為長索的選項，說明它能消耗能量、使斜索頻率與結構模態錯開並提高平面內勁度。交叉索的缺點是外觀、施工與維護較複雜，且交叉索本身在大振幅時可能鬆弛再拉緊而受衝擊，連接件要能承受反覆的拉力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「交叉索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Cross-ties are thin cables or links fitted between neighbouring stays in the same plane, joining them into a network. A long stay is divided into shorter segments, raising the frequency of the lowest modes and moving easily excited low-frequency vibration upward; the stays’ frequencies are no longer independent but restrain one another and spread vibration energy through the network. A supplier lists cross-ties as an option for longer stays, citing energy dissipation, decorrelation of stay frequencies from structural modes and higher in-plane stiffness. The drawbacks are appearance, construction and maintenance complexity, and ties that slacken and re-tension under large amplitudes take shock loads, so connectors must withstand repeated tension. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Cross-ties” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：張緊弦頻率與段長成反比。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Taut-string frequency is inversely proportional to segment length.","failure":"常見誤解：「交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「交叉索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Cross-ties”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-17-k1","title":"交叉索：把單根長索變成索網","titleEn":"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network","text":"交叉索是在同一索面相鄰斜索之間加裝細索或連桿，把它們連成網。單根長索被分成較短的段落，低階模態的頻率提高，原本容易被雨風或橋面運動激發的低頻振動被移到較高頻率；不同斜索的頻率也不再各自獨立，彼此牽制，振動能量在網中分散。","textEn":"Cross-ties are thin cables or links fitted between neighbouring stays in the same plane, joining them into a network. A long stay is divided into shorter segments, raising the frequency of the lowest modes and moving easily excited low-frequency vibration upward; the stays’ frequencies are no longer independent but restrain one another and spread vibration energy through the network.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交叉索：把單根長索變成索網」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network\" is correct?","options":["交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。","內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。","交叉索是在同一索面相鄰斜索之間加裝細索或連桿，把它們連成網。"],"optionsEn":["Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation.","Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.","Cross-ties are thin cables or links fitted between neighbouring stays in the same plane, joining them into a network."],"answer":2,"explanation":"交叉索是在同一索面相鄰斜索之間加裝細索或連桿，把它們連成網。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Cross-ties are thin cables or links fitted between neighbouring stays in the same plane, joining them into a network. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b051-v13-18","title":"交叉索：把單根長索變成索網：定量估算","titleEn":"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「交叉索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cross-ties” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：張緊弦頻率與段長成反比。索長 250 m、第一頻率 0.25 Hz，若在中點以剛性足夠的交叉索固定，局部段長 125 m，局部第一頻率約提高到 0.25×2 = 0.5 Hz；若在三分點各加一道，段長約 83 m，局部頻率約 0.75 Hz。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Taut-string frequency is inversely proportional to segment length. A 250 m stay with a 0.25 Hz first frequency, fixed at mid-length by a sufficiently stiff cross-tie, has 125 m segments with a local first frequency of about 0.25×2 = 0.5 Hz; ties at both third points give segments of about 83 m and about 0.75 Hz. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以索網模型計算加裝交叉索後的模態與頻率，並模擬大振幅時交叉索是否鬆弛；安裝時以預拉力確保交叉索在正常振幅下保持受拉，完成後量測索網的頻率與阻尼，並定期檢查連接件磨耗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compute modes and frequencies of the network with cross-ties and simulate whether ties slacken at large amplitudes; pretension ties so they remain taut at normal amplitudes, measure network frequencies and damping after installation, and inspect connector wear periodically.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"張緊弦頻率與段長成反比。索長 250 m、第一頻率 0.25 Hz，若在中點以剛性足夠的交叉索固定，局部段長 125 m，局部第一頻率約提高到 0.25×2 = 0.5 Hz；若在三分點各加一道，段長約 83 m，局部頻率約 0.75 Hz。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Taut-string frequency is inversely proportional to segment length. A 250 m stay with a 0.25 Hz first frequency, fixed at mid-length by a sufficiently stiff cross-tie, has 125 m segments with a local first frequency of about 0.25×2 = 0.5 Hz; ties at both third points give segments of about 83 m and about 0.75 Hz. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「交叉索：把單根長索變成索網」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network\", which statement holds?","options":["張緊弦頻率與段長成反比。","阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。","阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。"],"optionsEn":["Taut-string frequency is inversely proportional to segment length.","A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge.","Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"張緊弦頻率與段長成反比。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Taut-string frequency is inversely proportional to segment length. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b051-v13-19","title":"交叉索：把單根長索變成索網：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「交叉索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cross-ties” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以索網模型計算加裝交叉索後的模態與頻率，並模擬大振幅時交叉索是否鬆弛；安裝時以預拉力確保交叉索在正常振幅下保持受拉，完成後量測索網的頻率與阻尼，並定期檢查連接件磨耗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compute modes and frequencies of the network with cross-ties and simulate whether ties slacken at large amplitudes; pretension ties so they remain taut at normal amplitudes, measure network frequencies and damping after installation, and inspect connector wear periodically. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交叉索的設計要包含預拉力、連接件疲勞與斷裂後的掉落防護，並在交接文件中列出每道交叉索的位置、預拉力與檢查方法；景觀影響要在設計初期與業主溝通。","observationEn":"Site practice: Cross-tie design should include pretension, connector fatigue and fall protection in case of rupture, with each tie’s position, pretension and inspection method listed in the handover documents; discuss visual impact with the owner early.","failure":"注意干擾：交叉索預拉力不足時，大振幅下反覆鬆弛再拉緊，產生衝擊力使連接件斷裂；若交叉索斷裂掉落，可能危及車道，且原本被抑制的振動會突然恢復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Insufficiently pretensioned ties slacken and snap taut repeatedly at large amplitudes, shock-loading connectors until they fail; a broken tie falling can endanger traffic, and the suppressed vibration suddenly returns. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以索網模型計算加裝交叉索後的模態與頻率，並模擬大振幅時交叉索是否鬆弛；安裝時以預拉力確保交叉索在正常振幅下保持受拉，完成後量測索網的頻率與阻尼，並定期檢查連接件磨耗。","textEn":"Compute modes and frequencies of the network with cross-ties and simulate whether ties slacken at large amplitudes; pretension ties so they remain taut at normal amplitudes, measure network frequencies and damping after installation, and inspect connector wear periodically.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交叉索的設計要包含預拉力、連接件疲勞與斷裂後的掉落防護，並在交接文件中列出每道交叉索的位置、預拉力與檢查方法；景觀影響要在設計初期與業主溝通。","textEn":"Cross-tie design should include pretension, connector fatigue and fall protection in case of rupture, with each tie’s position, pretension and inspection method listed in the handover documents; discuss visual impact with the owner early.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「交叉索：把單根長索變成索網」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以索網模型計算加裝交叉索後的模態與頻率，並模擬大振幅時交叉索是否鬆弛。","斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compute modes and frequencies of the network with cross-ties and simulate whether ties slacken at large amplitudes.","Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以索網模型計算加裝交叉索後的模態與頻率，並模擬大振幅時交叉索是否鬆弛；安裝時以預拉力確保交叉索在正常振幅下保持受拉，完成後量測索網的頻率與阻尼，並定期檢查連接件磨耗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compute modes and frequencies of the network with cross-ties and simulate whether ties slacken at large amplitudes; pretension ties so they remain taut at normal amplitudes, measure network frequencies and damping after installation, and inspect connector wear periodically. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b051-v13-20","title":"交叉索：把單根長索變成索網：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「交叉索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cross-ties” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"交叉索預拉力不足時，大振幅下反覆鬆弛再拉緊，產生衝擊力使連接件斷裂；若交叉索斷裂掉落，可能危及車道，且原本被抑制的振動會突然恢復。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Insufficiently pretensioned ties slacken and snap taut repeatedly at large amplitudes, shock-loading connectors until they fail; a broken tie falling can endanger traffic, and the suppressed vibration suddenly returns. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：交叉索的缺點是外觀、施工與維護較複雜，且交叉索本身在大振幅時可能鬆弛再拉緊而受衝擊，連接件要能承受反覆的拉力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The drawbacks are appearance, construction and maintenance complexity, and ties that slacken and re-tension under large amplitudes take shock loads, so connectors must withstand repeated tension.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"交叉索預拉力不足時，大振幅下反覆鬆弛再拉緊，產生衝擊力使連接件斷裂；若交叉索斷裂掉落，可能危及車道，且原本被抑制的振動會突然恢復。","textEn":"Insufficiently pretensioned ties slacken and snap taut repeatedly at large amplitudes, shock-loading connectors until they fail; a broken tie falling can endanger traffic, and the suppressed vibration suddenly returns.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「交叉索：把單根長索變成索網」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cross-ties: turning single long stays into a cable network\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。","交叉索預拉力不足時，大振幅下反覆鬆弛再拉緊，產生衝擊力使連接件斷裂；若交叉索斷裂掉落，可能危及車道，且原本被抑制的振動會突然恢復。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.","Insufficiently pretensioned ties slacken and snap taut repeatedly at large amplitudes, shock-loading connectors until they fail."],"answer":2,"explanation":"交叉索預拉力不足時，大振幅下反覆鬆弛再拉緊，產生衝擊力使連接件斷裂；若交叉索斷裂掉落，可能危及車道，且原本被抑制的振動會突然恢復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Insufficiently pretensioned ties slacken and snap taut repeatedly at large amplitudes, shock-loading connectors until they fail; a broken tie falling can endanger traffic, and the suppressed vibration suddenly returns. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b051-v13-21","title":"內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「導管內阻尼器」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Guide-pipe internal damper” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"較短的斜索常把阻尼器裝在錨具上方的導管內，外觀幾乎看不到。供應商公開的選型表依索長分級：內置彈性體阻尼器適用約 80 m 以下、行程約 ±10 mm；內置油壓阻尼器適用約 80 至 150 m、行程可達約 20 mm；超過約 300 m 的長索則用外置油壓阻尼器，行程可達約 500 mm 或依需求訂製。內置阻尼器距錨點很近，能提供的附加阻尼有限，而且它所在位置的振幅雖小，仍可能超過行程。安裝時導管與索的同心度必須準確，否則阻尼器偏心受力、磨耗加速，甚至在靜止時就已用掉部分行程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「導管內阻尼器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Shorter stays often have dampers inside the guide pipe above the anchorage, nearly invisible. A supplier’s public selection table grades them by cable length: internal elastomeric dampers for stays under about 80 m with about ±10 mm stroke; internal hydraulic dampers for about 80 to 150 m with up to about 20 mm; and external hydraulic dampers for stays over about 300 m with up to about 500 mm stroke or custom values. Internal dampers sit close to the anchorage, so their added damping is limited, and although amplitude there is small it can still exceed the stroke. During installation the guide pipe must be concentric with the stay, or the damper is loaded eccentrically, wears faster and may use part of its stroke even at rest. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Guide-pipe internal damper” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：第一模態振型 y(x) = A·sin(πx/L)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: First-mode shape y(x) = A·sin(πx/L).","failure":"常見誤解：「內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「導管內阻尼器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Guide-pipe internal damper”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-21-k1","title":"內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差","titleEn":"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance","text":"較短的斜索常把阻尼器裝在錨具上方的導管內，外觀幾乎看不到。供應商公開的選型表依索長分級：內置彈性體阻尼器適用約 80 m 以下、行程約 ±10 mm；內置油壓阻尼器適用約 80 至 150 m、行程可達約 20 mm；超過約 300 m 的長索則用外置油壓阻尼器，行程可達約 500 mm 或依需求訂製。","textEn":"Shorter stays often have dampers inside the guide pipe above the anchorage, nearly invisible. A supplier’s public selection table grades them by cable length: internal elastomeric dampers for stays under about 80 m with about ±10 mm stroke; internal hydraulic dampers for about 80 to 150 m with up to about 20 mm; and external hydraulic dampers for stays over about 300 m with up to about 500 mm stroke or custom values.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance\" is correct?","options":["較短的斜索常把阻尼器裝在錨具上方的導管內，外觀幾乎看不到。","內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。","只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。"],"optionsEn":["Shorter stays often have dampers inside the guide pipe above the anchorage, nearly invisible.","Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.","An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"較短的斜索常把阻尼器裝在錨具上方的導管內，外觀幾乎看不到。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Shorter stays often have dampers inside the guide pipe above the anchorage, nearly invisible. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b051-v13-22","title":"內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差：定量估算","titleEn":"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導管內阻尼器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Guide-pipe internal damper” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：第一模態振型 y(x) = A·sin(πx/L)。若跨中振幅 A = 0.5 m、阻尼器在 x/L = 0.02，y = 0.5×sin(0.0628) ≈ 0.0314 m ≈ 31 mm，超過約 ±10 mm 的彈性體阻尼器行程，需改用較大行程的油壓型或限制振幅的配套措施。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: First-mode shape y(x) = A·sin(πx/L). With mid-span amplitude A = 0.5 m and the damper at x/L = 0.02, y = 0.5×sin(0.0628) ≈ 0.0314 m ≈ 31 mm, beyond the roughly ±10 mm stroke of an elastomeric damper, so a longer-stroke hydraulic type or complementary amplitude limits are needed. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：安裝前量測導管與錨具軸線的偏差，確認在容許範圍；安裝後檢查阻尼器靜止位置是否在行程中央，並以人工激振確認阻尼器在設計振幅下不撞到行程極限；每次檢查記錄阻尼器的磨耗與漏油狀況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before installation measure misalignment between guide pipe and anchorage axis against tolerance; afterwards check that the damper rests at mid-stroke and confirm by manual excitation that it does not hit its stroke limits at design amplitude; record wear and leakage at each inspection.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"第一模態振型 y(x) = A·sin(πx/L)。若跨中振幅 A = 0.5 m、阻尼器在 x/L = 0.02，y = 0.5×sin(0.0628) ≈ 0.0314 m ≈ 31 mm，超過約 ±10 mm 的彈性體阻尼器行程，需改用較大行程的油壓型或限制振幅的配套措施。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"First-mode shape y(x) = A·sin(πx/L). With mid-span amplitude A = 0.5 m and the damper at x/L = 0.02, y = 0.5×sin(0.0628) ≈ 0.0314 m ≈ 31 mm, beyond the roughly ±10 mm stroke of an elastomeric damper, so a longer-stroke hydraulic type or complementary amplitude limits are needed. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance\", which statement holds?","options":["斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。","第一模態振型 y(x) = A·sin(πx/L)。","雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。"],"optionsEn":["Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.","First-mode shape y(x) = A·sin(πx/L).","Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"第一模態振型 y(x) = A·sin(πx/L)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"First-mode shape y(x) = A·sin(πx/L). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b051-v13-23","title":"內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導管內阻尼器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Guide-pipe internal damper” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"安裝前量測導管與錨具軸線的偏差，確認在容許範圍；安裝後檢查阻尼器靜止位置是否在行程中央，並以人工激振確認阻尼器在設計振幅下不撞到行程極限；每次檢查記錄阻尼器的磨耗與漏油狀況。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before installation measure misalignment between guide pipe and anchorage axis against tolerance; afterwards check that the damper rests at mid-stroke and confirm by manual excitation that it does not hit its stroke limits at design amplitude; record wear and leakage at each inspection. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工規範要訂出導管定位公差、阻尼器安裝時的索力與溫度條件，以及安裝後的行程位置檢查；維護手冊應規定開啟導管蓋檢查阻尼器的週期與判定標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction specification should set guide-pipe positioning tolerance, the stay force and temperature at damper installation and the post-installation stroke check; the maintenance manual should set intervals and criteria for opening guide-pipe covers to inspect dampers.","failure":"注意干擾：導管偏心造成阻尼器單側磨耗，數年內失效；行程不足時阻尼器在大振幅下撞擊止擋，反而成為衝擊來源，並把彎曲應力集中在錨口附近的鋼絞線。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An eccentric guide pipe wears the damper on one side until it fails within a few years; insufficient stroke lets the damper hit its stops at large amplitude, becoming a source of impact and concentrating bending stress in strands near the anchor exit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"安裝前量測導管與錨具軸線的偏差，確認在容許範圍；安裝後檢查阻尼器靜止位置是否在行程中央，並以人工激振確認阻尼器在設計振幅下不撞到行程極限；每次檢查記錄阻尼器的磨耗與漏油狀況。","textEn":"Before installation measure misalignment between guide pipe and anchorage axis against tolerance; afterwards check that the damper rests at mid-stroke and confirm by manual excitation that it does not hit its stroke limits at design amplitude; record wear and leakage at each inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工規範要訂出導管定位公差、阻尼器安裝時的索力與溫度條件，以及安裝後的行程位置檢查；維護手冊應規定開啟導管蓋檢查阻尼器的週期與判定標準。","textEn":"The construction specification should set guide-pipe positioning tolerance, the stay force and temperature at damper installation and the post-installation stroke check; the maintenance manual should set intervals and criteria for opening guide-pipe covers to inspect dampers.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。","安裝前量測導管與錨具軸線的偏差，確認在容許範圍。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.","Before installation measure misalignment between guide pipe and anchorage axis against tolerance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"安裝前量測導管與錨具軸線的偏差，確認在容許範圍；安裝後檢查阻尼器靜止位置是否在行程中央，並以人工激振確認阻尼器在設計振幅下不撞到行程極限；每次檢查記錄阻尼器的磨耗與漏油狀況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before installation measure misalignment between guide pipe and anchorage axis against tolerance; afterwards check that the damper rests at mid-stroke and confirm by manual excitation that it does not hit its stroke limits at design amplitude; record wear and leakage at each inspection. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b051-v13-24","title":"內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導管內阻尼器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Guide-pipe internal damper” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"導管偏心造成阻尼器單側磨耗，數年內失效；行程不足時阻尼器在大振幅下撞擊止擋，反而成為衝擊來源，並把彎曲應力集中在錨口附近的鋼絞線。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An eccentric guide pipe wears the damper on one side until it fails within a few years; insufficient stroke lets the damper hit its stops at large amplitude, becoming a source of impact and concentrating bending stress in strands near the anchor exit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：安裝時導管與索的同心度必須準確，否則阻尼器偏心受力、磨耗加速，甚至在靜止時就已用掉部分行程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: During installation the guide pipe must be concentric with the stay, or the damper is loaded eccentrically, wears faster and may use part of its stroke even at rest.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"導管偏心造成阻尼器單側磨耗，數年內失效；行程不足時阻尼器在大振幅下撞擊止擋，反而成為衝擊來源，並把彎曲應力集中在錨口附近的鋼絞線。","textEn":"An eccentric guide pipe wears the damper on one side until it fails within a few years; insufficient stroke lets the damper hit its stops at large amplitude, becoming a source of impact and concentrating bending stress in strands near the anchor exit.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「內置阻尼器的選型、行程與安裝公差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Internal damper selection, stroke and installation tolerance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["導管偏心造成阻尼器單側磨耗，數年內失效；行程不足時阻尼器在大振幅下撞擊止擋，反而成為衝擊來源，並把彎曲應力集中在錨口附近的鋼絞線。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。"],"optionsEn":["An eccentric guide pipe wears the damper on one side until it fails within a few years.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導管偏心造成阻尼器單側磨耗，數年內失效；行程不足時阻尼器在大振幅下撞擊止擋，反而成為衝擊來源，並把彎曲應力集中在錨口附近的鋼絞線。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An eccentric guide pipe wears the damper on one side until it fails within a few years; insufficient stroke lets the damper hit its stops at large amplitude, becoming a source of impact and concentrating bending stress in strands near the anchor exit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b051-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨」與「以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain\" and \"Accepting added damping by free decay\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b051-v13-25","title":"現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「雨量計與斜索加速度計」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rain gauge and stay accelerometers” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"要確認斜索振動是否為雨風振動、判斷對策是否有效，最可靠的證據是現場同步資料。代表性斜索上裝雙軸加速度計，記錄平面內與平面外振動；橋上設超音波風速計量測風速風向，再加雨量計記錄降雨強度。只有當大振幅與中等風速、特定風向及降雨同時出現，才能歸因於雨風振動；若大振幅出現在無雨強風時，可能是抖振、乾索馳振或橋面運動引起的參數共振，對策也不同。長期資料還能告訴工程師哪些索最容易振動，作為優先加裝阻尼器的依據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「雨量計與斜索加速度計」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The most reliable evidence of whether stay vibration is rain–wind induced, and whether remedies work, is synchronised field data. Biaxial accelerometers on representative stays record in-plane and out-of-plane motion; an ultrasonic anemometer on the deck measures wind speed and direction; a rain gauge logs rainfall intensity. Only when large amplitudes coincide with moderate wind, a particular direction and rainfall can the motion be attributed to rain–wind excitation; large amplitudes in strong dry wind may instead be buffeting, dry galloping or parametric resonance from deck motion, needing different remedies. Long-term data also show which stays vibrate most readily, setting priorities for damper retrofits. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Rain gauge and stay accelerometers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：由加速度換算振幅 A = a/(2πf)²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Amplitude from acceleration A = a/(2πf)².","failure":"常見誤解：「只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「雨量計與斜索加速度計」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Rain gauge and stay accelerometers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-25-k1","title":"現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨","titleEn":"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain","text":"要確認斜索振動是否為雨風振動、判斷對策是否有效，最可靠的證據是現場同步資料。代表性斜索上裝雙軸加速度計，記錄平面內與平面外振動；橋上設超音波風速計量測風速風向，再加雨量計記錄降雨強度。","textEn":"The most reliable evidence of whether stay vibration is rain–wind induced, and whether remedies work, is synchronised field data. Biaxial accelerometers on representative stays record in-plane and out-of-plane motion; an ultrasonic anemometer on the deck measures wind speed and direction; a rain gauge logs rainfall intensity.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain\" is correct?","options":["只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。","要確認斜索振動是否為雨風振動、判斷對策是否有效，最可靠的證據是現場同步資料。","阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。"],"optionsEn":["An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration.","The most reliable evidence of whether stay vibration is rain–wind induced, and whether remedies work, is synchronised field data.","A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"要確認斜索振動是否為雨風振動、判斷對策是否有效，最可靠的證據是現場同步資料。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The most reliable evidence of whether stay vibration is rain–wind induced, and whether remedies work, is synchronised field data. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b051-v13-26","title":"現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨：定量估算","titleEn":"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雨量計與斜索加速度計」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rain gauge and stay accelerometers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：由加速度換算振幅 A = a/(2πf)²。若加速度峰值 a = 5 m/s²、頻率 f = 1.1 Hz，(2π×1.1)² ≈ 47.8，A ≈ 5/47.8 ≈ 0.105 m，即約 105 mm；同樣加速度在 3.3 Hz 時振幅只有約 12 mm，所以必須同時看頻率才能判讀振幅。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Amplitude from acceleration A = a/(2πf)². For a peak a = 5 m/s² at f = 1.1 Hz, (2π×1.1)² ≈ 47.8 and A ≈ 5/47.8 ≈ 0.105 m, about 105 mm; the same acceleration at 3.3 Hz is only about 12 mm, so frequency must be read with acceleration to judge amplitude. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認各感測器時間同步、加速度計方向與安裝位置有照片紀錄；以事件觸發保存原始資料，並用頻譜與時間歷程同時判讀主要振動頻率、振幅與持續時間，與風速、風向、雨量做關聯分析。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm time synchronisation across sensors and record accelerometer orientation and mounting position with photographs; store raw data on event triggers and read dominant frequency, amplitude and duration from both spectra and time histories, correlating them with wind speed, direction and rainfall.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"由加速度換算振幅 A = a/(2πf)²。若加速度峰值 a = 5 m/s²、頻率 f = 1.1 Hz，(2π×1.1)² ≈ 47.8，A ≈ 5/47.8 ≈ 0.105 m，即約 105 mm；同樣加速度在 3.3 Hz 時振幅只有約 12 mm，所以必須同時看頻率才能判讀振幅。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Amplitude from acceleration A = a/(2πf)². For a peak a = 5 m/s² at f = 1.1 Hz, (2π×1.1)² ≈ 47.8 and A ≈ 5/47.8 ≈ 0.105 m, about 105 mm; the same acceleration at 3.3 Hz is only about 12 mm, so frequency must be read with acceleration to judge amplitude. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。","斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。","由加速度換算振幅 A = a/(2πf)²。"],"optionsEn":["Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed.","Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration.","Amplitude from acceleration A = a/(2πf)²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"由加速度換算振幅 A = a/(2πf)²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Amplitude from acceleration A = a/(2πf)². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b051-v13-27","title":"現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雨量計與斜索加速度計」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rain gauge and stay accelerometers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認各感測器時間同步、加速度計方向與安裝位置有照片紀錄；以事件觸發保存原始資料，並用頻譜與時間歷程同時判讀主要振動頻率、振幅與持續時間，與風速、風向、雨量做關聯分析。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm time synchronisation across sensors and record accelerometer orientation and mounting position with photographs; store raw data on event triggers and read dominant frequency, amplitude and duration from both spectra and time histories, correlating them with wind speed, direction and rainfall. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測計畫要列出感測器清單、取樣率、觸發條件與資料保存期限，並在通車初期至少涵蓋一個完整的風雨季節；監測報告要把事件依機制分類，作為對策設計與驗收的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: The monitoring plan should list sensors, sampling rates, trigger conditions and data retention, covering at least one full wind-and-rain season after opening; reports should classify events by mechanism as the basis for remedy design and acceptance.","failure":"注意干擾：若沒有雨量計，所有大振幅事件都無法分類，可能對錯誤的機制下對策；加速度計方向記錄錯誤會把平面內與平面外振動混淆，誤判阻尼器的效果。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without a rain gauge, large-amplitude events cannot be classified, inviting remedies for the wrong mechanism; misrecorded accelerometer orientation confuses in-plane and out-of-plane motion and misjudges damper effectiveness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認各感測器時間同步、加速度計方向與安裝位置有照片紀錄；以事件觸發保存原始資料，並用頻譜與時間歷程同時判讀主要振動頻率、振幅與持續時間，與風速、風向、雨量做關聯分析。","textEn":"Confirm time synchronisation across sensors and record accelerometer orientation and mounting position with photographs; store raw data on event triggers and read dominant frequency, amplitude and duration from both spectra and time histories, correlating them with wind speed, direction and rainfall.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測計畫要列出感測器清單、取樣率、觸發條件與資料保存期限，並在通車初期至少涵蓋一個完整的風雨季節；監測報告要把事件依機制分類，作為對策設計與驗收的依據。","textEn":"The monitoring plan should list sensors, sampling rates, trigger conditions and data retention, covering at least one full wind-and-rain season after opening; reports should classify events by mechanism as the basis for remedy design and acceptance.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain\"?","options":["確認各感測器時間同步、加速度計方向與安裝位置有照片紀錄。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Confirm time synchronisation across sensors and record accelerometer orientation and mounting position with photographs.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest."],"answer":0,"explanation":"確認各感測器時間同步、加速度計方向與安裝位置有照片紀錄；以事件觸發保存原始資料，並用頻譜與時間歷程同時判讀主要振動頻率、振幅與持續時間，與風速、風向、雨量做關聯分析。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm time synchronisation across sensors and record accelerometer orientation and mounting position with photographs; store raw data on event triggers and read dominant frequency, amplitude and duration from both spectra and time histories, correlating them with wind speed, direction and rainfall. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b051-v13-28","title":"現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨：失效診斷","titleEn":"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雨量計與斜索加速度計」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rain gauge and stay accelerometers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沒有雨量計，所有大振幅事件都無法分類，可能對錯誤的機制下對策；加速度計方向記錄錯誤會把平面內與平面外振動混淆，誤判阻尼器的效果。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without a rain gauge, large-amplitude events cannot be classified, inviting remedies for the wrong mechanism; misrecorded accelerometer orientation confuses in-plane and out-of-plane motion and misjudges damper effectiveness. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：長期資料還能告訴工程師哪些索最容易振動，作為優先加裝阻尼器的依據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Long-term data also show which stays vibrate most readily, setting priorities for damper retrofits.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沒有雨量計，所有大振幅事件都無法分類，可能對錯誤的機制下對策；加速度計方向記錄錯誤會把平面內與平面外振動混淆，誤判阻尼器的效果。","textEn":"Without a rain gauge, large-amplitude events cannot be classified, inviting remedies for the wrong mechanism; misrecorded accelerometer orientation confuses in-plane and out-of-plane motion and misjudges damper effectiveness.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「現場監測：同步記錄振動、風與雨」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Field monitoring: synchronised vibration, wind and rain\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若沒有雨量計，所有大振幅事件都無法分類，可能對錯誤的機制下對策；加速度計方向記錄錯誤會把平面內與平面外振動混淆，誤判阻尼器的效果。","阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Without a rain gauge, large-amplitude events cannot be classified, inviting remedies for the wrong mechanism.","A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若沒有雨量計，所有大振幅事件都無法分類，可能對錯誤的機制下對策；加速度計方向記錄錯誤會把平面內與平面外振動混淆，誤判阻尼器的效果。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without a rain gauge, large-amplitude events cannot be classified, inviting remedies for the wrong mechanism; misrecorded accelerometer orientation confuses in-plane and out-of-plane motion and misjudges damper effectiveness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b051-v13-29","title":"以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Accepting added damping by free decay: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「自由衰減試驗」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Free-decay test” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"阻尼器或交叉索裝好之後，必須以現場試驗證明斜索真的得到足夠的阻尼。最常用的是自由衰減試驗：以人工或拉繩把索拉到一定振幅後放開，記錄振幅逐週期遞減的過程，用對數遞減率換算阻尼比。試驗要針對目標模態激振，並在低風、無雨時進行，以免外力干擾衰減曲線；振幅也要接近實際關心的範圍，因為阻尼器的摩擦與非線性會讓小振幅與大振幅的阻尼不同。驗收時把量到的阻尼代回史庫頓數，確認達到設計門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「自由衰減試驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After dampers or cross-ties are fitted, field tests must prove the stay actually has enough damping. The commonest is the free-decay test: pull the stay to an amplitude by hand or rope, release it and record the amplitude decreasing cycle by cycle, converting the logarithmic decrement to a damping ratio. The test should excite the target mode, in low wind and no rain so external forces do not distort the decay, and at amplitudes near the range of interest, because damper friction and nonlinearity make damping differ between small and large amplitudes. Acceptance substitutes the measured damping into the Scruton number to confirm the design threshold is met. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Free-decay test” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Logarithmic decrement δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n).","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「自由衰減試驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Free-decay test”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-29-k1","title":"以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼","titleEn":"Accepting added damping by free decay","text":"阻尼器或交叉索裝好之後，必須以現場試驗證明斜索真的得到足夠的阻尼。最常用的是自由衰減試驗：以人工或拉繩把索拉到一定振幅後放開，記錄振幅逐週期遞減的過程，用對數遞減率換算阻尼比。","textEn":"After dampers or cross-ties are fitted, field tests must prove the stay actually has enough damping. The commonest is the free-decay test: pull the stay to an amplitude by hand or rope, release it and record the amplitude decreasing cycle by cycle, converting the logarithmic decrement to a damping ratio.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Accepting added damping by free decay\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。","斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。","阻尼器或交叉索裝好之後，必須以現場試驗證明斜索真的得到足夠的阻尼。"],"optionsEn":["A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge.","Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.","After dampers or cross-ties are fitted, field tests must prove the stay actually has enough damping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻尼器或交叉索裝好之後，必須以現場試驗證明斜索真的得到足夠的阻尼。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After dampers or cross-ties are fitted, field tests must prove the stay actually has enough damping. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b051-v13-30","title":"以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼：定量估算","titleEn":"Accepting added damping by free decay: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「自由衰減試驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Free-decay test” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n)。振幅 10 個週期由 100 mm 降到 30 mm：δ = ln(100/30)/10 ≈ 0.120，ζ = δ/(2π) ≈ 1.92%。代入單元 2 的參數，Sc = 60×0.0192/0.032 ≈ 36，高於約 10 的門檻。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Logarithmic decrement δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n). Amplitude falling from 100 mm to 30 mm in 10 cycles gives δ = ln(100/30)/10 ≈ 0.120 and ζ = δ/(2π) ≈ 1.92%. With unit 2’s parameters, Sc = 60×0.0192/0.032 ≈ 36, above the threshold of about 10. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每根受測索至少重複三次並取平均，檢查衰減曲線是否為單一指數（若出現轉折，可能是阻尼器摩擦或拍頻）；同時記錄風速與溫度，並把結果與阻尼器安裝前的基準比較，列入驗收報告。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat at least three times per stay and average, checking that the decay is a single exponential (a kink may indicate damper friction or beating between modes); record wind and temperature and compare with the pre-installation baseline in the acceptance report.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n)。振幅 10 個週期由 100 mm 降到 30 mm：δ = ln(100/30)/10 ≈ 0.120，ζ = δ/(2π) ≈ 1.92%。代入單元 2 的參數，Sc = 60×0.0192/0.032 ≈ 36，高於約 10 的門檻。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Logarithmic decrement δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n). Amplitude falling from 100 mm to 30 mm in 10 cycles gives δ = ln(100/30)/10 ≈ 0.120 and ζ = δ/(2π) ≈ 1.92%. With unit 2’s parameters, Sc = 60×0.0192/0.032 ≈ 36, above the threshold of about 10. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Accepting added damping by free decay\", which statement holds?","options":["對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n)。","雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。","套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。"],"optionsEn":["Logarithmic decrement δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n).","Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration.","The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"對數遞減率 δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Logarithmic decrement δ = (1/n)·ln(A₀/A_n). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b051-v13-31","title":"以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Accepting added damping by free decay: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「自由衰減試驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Free-decay test” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每根受測索至少重複三次並取平均，檢查衰減曲線是否為單一指數（若出現轉折，可能是阻尼器摩擦或拍頻）；同時記錄風速與溫度，並把結果與阻尼器安裝前的基準比較，列入驗收報告。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat at least three times per stay and average, checking that the decay is a single exponential (a kink may indicate damper friction or beating between modes); record wind and temperature and compare with the pre-installation baseline in the acceptance report. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：驗收計畫要規定受測索的抽樣比例、激振方法、振幅範圍、天候條件與允收值；高空激振作業須使用經核可的設備與安全措施，由主管工程師核准後執行。","observationEn":"Site practice: The acceptance plan should set the sampling rate of stays tested, excitation method, amplitude range, weather conditions and acceptance values; excitation at height must use approved equipment and safety measures, authorised by the responsible engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：在有風時做試驗，風的持續輸入使衰減變慢，量到的阻尼偏低而誤判不合格；或在兩個相近模態同時被激發時出現拍頻，用單一指數擬合會得到錯誤的阻尼值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing in wind slows the decay through continued input and understates damping, causing a false failure; exciting two close modes together produces beating, and a single exponential fit gives the wrong damping. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每根受測索至少重複三次並取平均，檢查衰減曲線是否為單一指數（若出現轉折，可能是阻尼器摩擦或拍頻）；同時記錄風速與溫度，並把結果與阻尼器安裝前的基準比較，列入驗收報告。","textEn":"Repeat at least three times per stay and average, checking that the decay is a single exponential (a kink may indicate damper friction or beating between modes); record wind and temperature and compare with the pre-installation baseline in the acceptance report.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"驗收計畫要規定受測索的抽樣比例、激振方法、振幅範圍、天候條件與允收值；高空激振作業須使用經核可的設備與安全措施，由主管工程師核准後執行。","textEn":"The acceptance plan should set the sampling rate of stays tested, excitation method, amplitude range, weather conditions and acceptance values; excitation at height must use approved equipment and safety measures, authorised by the responsible engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Accepting added damping by free decay\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","每根受測索至少重複三次並取平均，檢查衰減曲線是否為單一指數（若出現轉折，可能是阻尼器摩擦或拍頻）。","交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Repeat at least three times per stay and average, checking that the decay is a single exponential (a kink may indicate damper friction or beating between modes).","Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每根受測索至少重複三次並取平均，檢查衰減曲線是否為單一指數（若出現轉折，可能是阻尼器摩擦或拍頻）；同時記錄風速與溫度，並把結果與阻尼器安裝前的基準比較，列入驗收報告。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat at least three times per stay and average, checking that the decay is a single exponential (a kink may indicate damper friction or beating between modes); record wind and temperature and compare with the pre-installation baseline in the acceptance report. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b051-v13-32","title":"以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼：失效診斷","titleEn":"Accepting added damping by free decay: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「自由衰減試驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Free-decay test” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在有風時做試驗，風的持續輸入使衰減變慢，量到的阻尼偏低而誤判不合格；或在兩個相近模態同時被激發時出現拍頻，用單一指數擬合會得到錯誤的阻尼值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing in wind slows the decay through continued input and understates damping, causing a false failure; exciting two close modes together produces beating, and a single exponential fit gives the wrong damping. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：驗收時把量到的阻尼代回史庫頓數，確認達到設計門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Acceptance substitutes the measured damping into the Scruton number to confirm the design threshold is met.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器有出廠試驗報告，就不需要在橋上做衰減試驗。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A damper with a factory test report needs no decay test on the bridge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在有風時做試驗，風的持續輸入使衰減變慢，量到的阻尼偏低而誤判不合格；或在兩個相近模態同時被激發時出現拍頻，用單一指數擬合會得到錯誤的阻尼值。","textEn":"Testing in wind slows the decay through continued input and understates damping, causing a false failure; exciting two close modes together produces beating, and a single exponential fit gives the wrong damping.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「以自由衰減驗收附加阻尼」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Accepting added damping by free decay\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。","在有風時做試驗，風的持續輸入使衰減變慢，量到的阻尼偏低而誤判不合格；或在兩個相近模態同時被激發時出現拍頻，用單一指數擬合會得到錯誤的阻尼值。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.","Testing in wind slows the decay through continued input and understates damping, causing a false failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在有風時做試驗，風的持續輸入使衰減變慢，量到的阻尼偏低而誤判不合格；或在兩個相近模態同時被激發時出現拍頻，用單一指數擬合會得到錯誤的阻尼值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing in wind slows the decay through continued input and understates damping, causing a false failure; exciting two close modes together produces beating, and a single exponential fit gives the wrong damping. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b051-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞」與「阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration\" and \"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b051-v13-33","title":"振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「錨口導向器」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Anchor-exit deviator” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"斜索振動時，索在錨具出口處被迫轉角，鋼絞線在此承受軸向應力之外的彎曲應力；振動頻率約 1 Hz 的雨風振動每小時就有數千次循環，累積多年後可能達到疲勞範圍。錨具出口通常設有導向器或濾彎裝置，讓轉角分散在一段長度上，降低局部曲率；供應商公開資料也提到為較大型鋼腱設置彎曲濾波器或導向器以限制彎曲應力。因此抑制振動不只是使用者感受的問題，而是保護錨口鋼絞線疲勞壽命的關鍵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「錨口導向器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When a stay vibrates, it is forced to rotate at the anchorage exit, and strands there see bending stress on top of axial stress; rain–wind vibration at about 1 Hz produces thousands of cycles per hour and over years can accumulate into the fatigue range. Anchor exits usually have deviators or bending filters that spread the rotation over a length and reduce local curvature; supplier material also mentions bending filters or deviators to limit bending stress in larger tendons. Suppressing vibration is therefore not just about user perception but key to protecting the fatigue life of strands at the anchor exit. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Anchor-exit deviator” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若某索每年有 50 小時處於 1.2 Hz 的雨風振動，年循環數 = 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000 次，20 年約 4.32×10⁶ 次，已達鋼材 S–N 曲線的高循環範圍；若加裝阻尼器使振動時數降為 5 小時，循環數降為十分之一。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If a stay spends 50 hours a year in rain–wind vibration at 1.2 Hz, the annual cycle count is 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000, about 4.32×10⁶ over 20 years, already in the high-cycle range of steel S–N curves; a damper retrofit cutting vibration to 5 hours a year reduces cycles tenfold.","failure":"常見誤解：「斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「錨口導向器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Anchor-exit deviator”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-33-k1","title":"振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞","titleEn":"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration","text":"斜索振動時，索在錨具出口處被迫轉角，鋼絞線在此承受軸向應力之外的彎曲應力；振動頻率約 1 Hz 的雨風振動每小時就有數千次循環，累積多年後可能達到疲勞範圍。錨具出口通常設有導向器或濾彎裝置，讓轉角分散在一段長度上，降低局部曲率；供應商公開資料也提到為較大型鋼腱設置彎曲濾波器或導向器以限制彎曲應力。","textEn":"When a stay vibrates, it is forced to rotate at the anchorage exit, and strands there see bending stress on top of axial stress; rain–wind vibration at about 1 Hz produces thousands of cycles per hour and over years can accumulate into the fatigue range. Anchor exits usually have deviators or bending filters that spread the rotation over a length and reduce local curvature; supplier material also mentions bending filters or deviators to limit bending stress in larger tendons.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration\" is correct?","options":["斜索振動時，索在錨具出口處被迫轉角，鋼絞線在此承受軸向應力之外的彎曲應力；振動頻率約 1 Hz 的雨風振動每小時就有數千次循環，累積多年後可能達到疲勞範圍。","斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。","阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。"],"optionsEn":["When a stay vibrates, it is forced to rotate at the anchorage exit, and strands there see bending stress on top of axial stress.","Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.","Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"斜索振動時，索在錨具出口處被迫轉角，鋼絞線在此承受軸向應力之外的彎曲應力；振動頻率約 1 Hz 的雨風振動每小時就有數千次循環，累積多年後可能達到疲勞範圍。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When a stay vibrates, it is forced to rotate at the anchorage exit, and strands there see bending stress on top of axial stress; rain–wind vibration at about 1 Hz produces thousands of cycles per hour and over years can accumulate into the fatigue range. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b051-v13-34","title":"振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞：定量估算","titleEn":"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「錨口導向器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Anchor-exit deviator” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若某索每年有 50 小時處於 1.2 Hz 的雨風振動，年循環數 = 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000 次，20 年約 4.32×10⁶ 次，已達鋼材 S–N 曲線的高循環範圍；若加裝阻尼器使振動時數降為 5 小時，循環數降為十分之一。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If a stay spends 50 hours a year in rain–wind vibration at 1.2 Hz, the annual cycle count is 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000, about 4.32×10⁶ over 20 years, already in the high-cycle range of steel S–N curves; a damper retrofit cutting vibration to 5 hours a year reduces cycles tenfold. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以錨口附近的應變計量測振動時的彎曲應變範圍，配合監測統計的振動時數，以 S–N 曲線與 Miner 法則估算累積損傷；定期打開錨具保護蓋檢查錨口附近的鋼絞線、夾片與導向器磨耗。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Gauge bending strain ranges near the anchor exit during vibration and combine with monitored vibration hours to estimate cumulative damage by S–N curves and Miner’s rule; periodically open anchorage caps to inspect strands, wedges and deviator wear near the exit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若某索每年有 50 小時處於 1.2 Hz 的雨風振動，年循環數 = 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000 次，20 年約 4.32×10⁶ 次，已達鋼材 S–N 曲線的高循環範圍；若加裝阻尼器使振動時數降為 5 小時，循環數降為十分之一。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"If a stay spends 50 hours a year in rain–wind vibration at 1.2 Hz, the annual cycle count is 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000, about 4.32×10⁶ over 20 years, already in the high-cycle range of steel S–N curves; a damper retrofit cutting vibration to 5 hours a year reduces cycles tenfold. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration\", which statement holds?","options":["斜索越重越粗就越穩定，所以只要加大索徑就能解決雨風振動。","若某索每年有 50 小時處於 1.2 Hz 的雨風振動，年循環數 = 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000 次，20 年約 4.32×10⁶ 次，已達鋼材 S–N 曲線的高循環範圍。","阻尼器裝在越靠近錨具的位置越好，因為那裡索最穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Heavier, thicker stays are always more stable, so a larger diameter solves rain–wind vibration.","If a stay spends 50 hours a year in rain–wind vibration at 1.2 Hz, the annual cycle count is 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000, about 4.32×10⁶ over 20 years, already in the high-cycle range of steel S–N curves.","Dampers work best right at the anchorage, where the stay is steadiest."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若某索每年有 50 小時處於 1.2 Hz 的雨風振動，年循環數 = 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000 次，20 年約 4.32×10⁶ 次，已達鋼材 S–N 曲線的高循環範圍；若加裝阻尼器使振動時數降為 5 小時，循環數降為十分之一。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If a stay spends 50 hours a year in rain–wind vibration at 1.2 Hz, the annual cycle count is 1.2×3,600×50 = 216,000, about 4.32×10⁶ over 20 years, already in the high-cycle range of steel S–N curves; a damper retrofit cutting vibration to 5 hours a year reduces cycles tenfold. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b051-v13-35","title":"振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「錨口導向器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Anchor-exit deviator” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以錨口附近的應變計量測振動時的彎曲應變範圍，配合監測統計的振動時數，以 S–N 曲線與 Miner 法則估算累積損傷；定期打開錨具保護蓋檢查錨口附近的鋼絞線、夾片與導向器磨耗。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Gauge bending strain ranges near the anchor exit during vibration and combine with monitored vibration hours to estimate cumulative damage by S–N curves and Miner’s rule; periodically open anchorage caps to inspect strands, wedges and deviator wear near the exit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：斜索系統的疲勞試驗要包含錨口轉角條件，導向器與濾彎裝置列為可檢查與可更換構件；監測系統應統計每根索的大振幅時數，超過門檻時排入錨口專項檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Stay-system fatigue tests should include anchor-exit rotation, with deviators and bending filters inspectable and replaceable; monitoring should count large-amplitude hours per stay and trigger a special anchor-exit inspection when a threshold is exceeded.","failure":"注意干擾：導向器缺失或磨損，錨口處鋼絞線在反覆彎曲下出現斷絲，斷絲又使剩餘鋼絞線受力增加；由於位置隱蔽，若不定期檢查，可能等到多股斷裂才被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A missing or worn deviator lets strands at the anchor exit break wires under repeated bending, raising force in the remaining strands; because the location is hidden, without regular inspection the damage may be found only after several strands have failed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以錨口附近的應變計量測振動時的彎曲應變範圍，配合監測統計的振動時數，以 S–N 曲線與 Miner 法則估算累積損傷；定期打開錨具保護蓋檢查錨口附近的鋼絞線、夾片與導向器磨耗。","textEn":"Gauge bending strain ranges near the anchor exit during vibration and combine with monitored vibration hours to estimate cumulative damage by S–N curves and Miner’s rule; periodically open anchorage caps to inspect strands, wedges and deviator wear near the exit.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"斜索系統的疲勞試驗要包含錨口轉角條件，導向器與濾彎裝置列為可檢查與可更換構件；監測系統應統計每根索的大振幅時數，超過門檻時排入錨口專項檢查。","textEn":"Stay-system fatigue tests should include anchor-exit rotation, with deviators and bending filters inspectable and replaceable; monitoring should count large-amplitude hours per stay and trigger a special anchor-exit inspection when a threshold is exceeded.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","內置阻尼器藏在導管裡，因此不需要檢查或維護。","以錨口附近的應變計量測振動時的彎曲應變範圍，配合監測統計的振動時數，以 S–N 曲線與 Miner 法則估算累積損傷。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Internal dampers are hidden in the guide pipe, so they need no inspection or maintenance.","Gauge bending strain ranges near the anchor exit during vibration and combine with monitored vibration hours to estimate cumulative damage by S–N curves and Miner’s rule."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以錨口附近的應變計量測振動時的彎曲應變範圍，配合監測統計的振動時數，以 S–N 曲線與 Miner 法則估算累積損傷；定期打開錨具保護蓋檢查錨口附近的鋼絞線、夾片與導向器磨耗。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Gauge bending strain ranges near the anchor exit during vibration and combine with monitored vibration hours to estimate cumulative damage by S–N curves and Miner’s rule; periodically open anchorage caps to inspect strands, wedges and deviator wear near the exit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b051-v13-36","title":"振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「錨口導向器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Anchor-exit deviator” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"導向器缺失或磨損，錨口處鋼絞線在反覆彎曲下出現斷絲，斷絲又使剩餘鋼絞線受力增加；由於位置隱蔽，若不定期檢查，可能等到多股斷裂才被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A missing or worn deviator lets strands at the anchor exit break wires under repeated bending, raising force in the remaining strands; because the location is hidden, without regular inspection the damage may be found only after several strands have failed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此抑制振動不只是使用者感受的問題，而是保護錨口鋼絞線疲勞壽命的關鍵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Suppressing vibration is therefore not just about user perception but key to protecting the fatigue life of strands at the anchor exit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斜索只承受軸向拉力，所以振動不會造成彎曲疲勞。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stays carry only axial tension, so vibration cannot cause bending fatigue.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"導向器缺失或磨損，錨口處鋼絞線在反覆彎曲下出現斷絲，斷絲又使剩餘鋼絞線受力增加；由於位置隱蔽，若不定期檢查，可能等到多股斷裂才被發現。","textEn":"A missing or worn deviator lets strands at the anchor exit break wires under repeated bending, raising force in the remaining strands; because the location is hidden, without regular inspection the damage may be found only after several strands have failed.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「振動造成的錨口彎曲疲勞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bending fatigue at the anchor exit from vibration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["導向器缺失或磨損，錨口處鋼絞線在反覆彎曲下出現斷絲，斷絲又使剩餘鋼絞線受力增加；由於位置隱蔽，若不定期檢查，可能等到多股斷裂才被發現。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。"],"optionsEn":["A missing or worn deviator lets strands at the anchor exit break wires under repeated bending, raising force in the remaining strands.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導向器缺失或磨損，錨口處鋼絞線在反覆彎曲下出現斷絲，斷絲又使剩餘鋼絞線受力增加；由於位置隱蔽，若不定期檢查，可能等到多股斷裂才被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A missing or worn deviator lets strands at the anchor exit break wires under repeated bending, raising force in the remaining strands; because the location is hidden, without regular inspection the damage may be found only after several strands have failed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b051-v13-37","title":"阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「阻尼器累積行程」如何影響斜張索雨風振動抑制的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damper cumulative stroke” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rain–wind vibration mitigation for stay cables”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"斜索阻尼器是長期反覆運動的機械元件，其耐久常以累積行程表示：供應商公開資料列出內置油壓阻尼器約 30 km、彈性體與外置油壓阻尼器約 100 km 的累積行程耐久。油壓阻尼器的密封會磨耗漏油，彈性體會老化硬化，連接銷與支架會鬆動。阻尼器失效時外觀往往看不出來，斜索卻會在下一場風雨中恢復振動。因此維護要結合定期檢查、監測資料中的振幅趨勢與事件後檢查，並把阻尼器的更換視為設計年限內的計畫性工作，而不是故障才處理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「阻尼器累積行程」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stay dampers are mechanical parts in constant reciprocating motion, and their durability is often expressed as cumulative stroke: a supplier lists about 30 km for internal hydraulic dampers and about 100 km for elastomeric and external hydraulic types. Hydraulic seals wear and leak, elastomers age and stiffen, and pins and brackets loosen. A failed damper often looks normal, yet the stay vibrates again in the next storm. Maintenance therefore combines periodic inspection, amplitude trends from monitoring and post-event checks, and treats damper replacement as planned work within the design life rather than a response to failure. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Damper cumulative stroke” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：阻尼器處振幅 5 mm、頻率 1.5 Hz 時，每週期行程 4×5 = 20 mm，每小時 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 5 mm amplitude at the damper and 1.5 Hz, each cycle travels 4×5 = 20 mm, about 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m per hour.","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「阻尼器累積行程」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Damper cumulative stroke”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-37-k1","title":"阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查","titleEn":"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks","text":"斜索阻尼器是長期反覆運動的機械元件，其耐久常以累積行程表示：供應商公開資料列出內置油壓阻尼器約 30 km、彈性體與外置油壓阻尼器約 100 km 的累積行程耐久。油壓阻尼器的密封會磨耗漏油，彈性體會老化硬化，連接銷與支架會鬆動。","textEn":"Stay dampers are mechanical parts in constant reciprocating motion, and their durability is often expressed as cumulative stroke: a supplier lists about 30 km for internal hydraulic dampers and about 100 km for elastomeric and external hydraulic types. Hydraulic seals wear and leak, elastomers age and stiffen, and pins and brackets loosen.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。","斜索阻尼器是長期反覆運動的機械元件，其耐久常以累積行程表示：供應商公開資料列出內置油壓阻尼器約 30 km、彈性體與外置油壓阻尼器約 100 km 的累積行程耐久。","雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。"],"optionsEn":["Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed.","Stay dampers are mechanical parts in constant reciprocating motion, and their durability is often expressed as cumulative stroke: a supplier lists about 30 km for internal hydraulic dampers and about 100 km for elastomeric and external hydraulic types.","Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"斜索阻尼器是長期反覆運動的機械元件，其耐久常以累積行程表示：供應商公開資料列出內置油壓阻尼器約 30 km、彈性體與外置油壓阻尼器約 100 km 的累積行程耐久。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stay dampers are mechanical parts in constant reciprocating motion, and their durability is often expressed as cumulative stroke: a supplier lists about 30 km for internal hydraulic dampers and about 100 km for elastomeric and external hydraulic types. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b051-v13-38","title":"阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查：定量估算","titleEn":"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「阻尼器累積行程」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damper cumulative stroke” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：阻尼器處振幅 5 mm、頻率 1.5 Hz 時，每週期行程 4×5 = 20 mm，每小時 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m。耐久 30 km 的阻尼器約可承受 30,000/108 ≈ 278 小時此強度的振動；100 km 型約 926 小時。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 5 mm amplitude at the damper and 1.5 Hz, each cycle travels 4×5 = 20 mm, about 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m per hour. A 30 km damper withstands about 30,000/108 ≈ 278 hours of such vibration; a 100 km type about 926 hours. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期目視檢查漏油、密封、支架與連接銷，並以監測資料估算每個阻尼器的累積行程，接近耐久值時排定更換；強風或颱風等事件後，抽查阻尼器行程極限是否被撞擊並複測代表性斜索的阻尼。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inspect periodically for leaks, seals, brackets and pins, estimate each damper’s cumulative stroke from monitoring data and schedule replacement as it nears its rating; after strong-wind events check whether stroke limits were struck and re-measure damping on representative stays.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"阻尼器處振幅 5 mm、頻率 1.5 Hz 時，每週期行程 4×5 = 20 mm，每小時 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m。耐久 30 km 的阻尼器約可承受 30,000/108 ≈ 278 小時此強度的振動；100 km 型約 926 小時。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With 5 mm amplitude at the damper and 1.5 Hz, each cycle travels 4×5 = 20 mm, about 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m per hour. A 30 km damper withstands about 30,000/108 ≈ 278 hours of such vibration; a 100 km type about 926 hours. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks\", which statement holds?","options":["套管表面處理越粗糙，抑振效果越好且沒有副作用。","交叉索只是把斜索綁在一起，不需要計算預拉力。","阻尼器處振幅 5 mm、頻率 1.5 Hz 時，每週期行程 4×5 = 20 mm，每小時 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m。"],"optionsEn":["The rougher the duct surface, the better the suppression, with no side effects.","Cross-ties just tie stays together and need no pretension calculation.","With 5 mm amplitude at the damper and 1.5 Hz, each cycle travels 4×5 = 20 mm, about 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m per hour."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻尼器處振幅 5 mm、頻率 1.5 Hz 時，每週期行程 4×5 = 20 mm，每小時 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 5 mm amplitude at the damper and 1.5 Hz, each cycle travels 4×5 = 20 mm, about 1.5×3,600×20 mm ≈ 108 m per hour. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b051-v13-39","title":"阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「阻尼器累積行程」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damper cumulative stroke” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期目視檢查漏油、密封、支架與連接銷，並以監測資料估算每個阻尼器的累積行程，接近耐久值時排定更換；強風或颱風等事件後，抽查阻尼器行程極限是否被撞擊並複測代表性斜索的阻尼。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inspect periodically for leaks, seals, brackets and pins, estimate each damper’s cumulative stroke from monitoring data and schedule replacement as it nears its rating; after strong-wind events check whether stroke limits were struck and re-measure damping on representative stays. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件要列出每個阻尼器的型號、設定係數、行程、耐久值、安裝日期與更換程序，並提供備品清單；維護紀錄應把阻尼器檢查結果與監測振幅趨勢放在同一資料庫中比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should list each damper’s type, coefficient setting, stroke, durability rating, installation date and replacement procedure, with a spares list; maintenance records should compare inspection findings with monitored amplitude trends in one database.","failure":"注意干擾：阻尼器漏油後阻尼係數下降，斜索在風雨中振動加劇，錨口疲勞與套管磨損加速；若沒有累積行程的估算，更換只能等到振動被民眾發現，屆時已累積可觀的疲勞損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A leaking damper loses coefficient, stay vibration grows in wind and rain, and anchor-exit fatigue and duct wear accelerate; without cumulative-stroke estimates replacement waits until the public notices vibration, by which time considerable fatigue damage has accrued. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期目視檢查漏油、密封、支架與連接銷，並以監測資料估算每個阻尼器的累積行程，接近耐久值時排定更換；強風或颱風等事件後，抽查阻尼器行程極限是否被撞擊並複測代表性斜索的阻尼。","textEn":"Inspect periodically for leaks, seals, brackets and pins, estimate each damper’s cumulative stroke from monitoring data and schedule replacement as it nears its rating; after strong-wind events check whether stroke limits were struck and re-measure damping on representative stays.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件要列出每個阻尼器的型號、設定係數、行程、耐久值、安裝日期與更換程序，並提供備品清單；維護紀錄應把阻尼器檢查結果與監測振幅趨勢放在同一資料庫中比對。","textEn":"Handover should list each damper’s type, coefficient setting, stroke, durability rating, installation date and replacement procedure, with a spares list; maintenance records should compare inspection findings with monitored amplitude trends in one database.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks\"?","options":["定期目視檢查漏油、密封、支架與連接銷，並以監測資料估算每個阻尼器的累積行程，接近耐久值時排定更換。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要有風速計和加速度計，就足以判斷斜索振動的原因。"],"optionsEn":["Inspect periodically for leaks, seals, brackets and pins, estimate each damper’s cumulative stroke from monitoring data and schedule replacement as it nears its rating.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","An anemometer and accelerometers are enough to diagnose the cause of stay vibration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"定期目視檢查漏油、密封、支架與連接銷，並以監測資料估算每個阻尼器的累積行程，接近耐久值時排定更換；強風或颱風等事件後，抽查阻尼器行程極限是否被撞擊並複測代表性斜索的阻尼。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inspect periodically for leaks, seals, brackets and pins, estimate each damper’s cumulative stroke from monitoring data and schedule replacement as it nears its rating; after strong-wind events check whether stroke limits were struck and re-measure damping on representative stays. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b051-v13-40","title":"阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查：失效診斷","titleEn":"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"prerequisiteIds":["b051-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「阻尼器累積行程」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damper cumulative stroke” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"阻尼器漏油後阻尼係數下降，斜索在風雨中振動加劇，錨口疲勞與套管磨損加速；若沒有累積行程的估算，更換只能等到振動被民眾發現，屆時已累積可觀的疲勞損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A leaking damper loses coefficient, stay vibration grows in wind and rain, and anchor-exit fatigue and duct wear accelerate; without cumulative-stroke estimates replacement waits until the public notices vibration, by which time considerable fatigue damage has accrued. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此維護要結合定期檢查、監測資料中的振幅趨勢與事件後檢查，並把阻尼器的更換視為設計年限內的計畫性工作，而不是故障才處理。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Maintenance therefore combines periodic inspection, amplitude trends from monitoring and post-event checks, and treats damper replacement as planned work within the design life rather than a response to failure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器是被動元件，裝好後可以使用到橋梁設計年限結束。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dampers are passive and last for the full design life once installed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b051-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"阻尼器漏油後阻尼係數下降，斜索在風雨中振動加劇，錨口疲勞與套管磨損加速；若沒有累積行程的估算，更換只能等到振動被民眾發現，屆時已累積可觀的疲勞損傷。","textEn":"A leaking damper loses coefficient, stay vibration grows in wind and rain, and anchor-exit fatigue and duct wear accelerate; without cumulative-stroke estimates replacement waits until the public notices vibration, by which time considerable fatigue damage has accrued.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]},{"id":"b051-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「阻尼器耐久、維護與事件後檢查」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Damper durability, maintenance and post-event checks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","阻尼器漏油後阻尼係數下降，斜索在風雨中振動加劇，錨口疲勞與套管磨損加速；若沒有累積行程的估算，更換只能等到振動被民眾發現，屆時已累積可觀的疲勞損傷。","雨水只是增加斜索重量，不會引起振動。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A leaking damper loses coefficient, stay vibration grows in wind and rain, and anchor-exit fatigue and duct wear accelerate.","Rain only adds weight to a stay and cannot cause vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"阻尼器漏油後阻尼係數下降，斜索在風雨中振動加劇，錨口疲勞與套管磨損加速；若沒有累積行程的估算，更換只能等到振動被民眾發現，屆時已累積可觀的疲勞損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A leaking damper loses coefficient, stay vibration grows in wind and rain, and anchor-exit fatigue and duct wear accelerate; without cumulative-stroke estimates replacement waits until the public notices vibration, by which time considerable fatigue damage has accrued. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-freyssinet-dampers","v13s-freyssinet-cable-systems","v13s-freyssinet-yavuz-selim","v13s-fib-bulletin-30","v13s-wiki-erasmusbrug"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
